etrieve a single webhook endpoint by ID"},"387":{"id":"/api/webhooks/listWebhookEndpoints","page_id":"/api/webhooks/listWebhookEndpoints","type":"page","content":"List webhook endpoints","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Pulsarr API","Webhooks"],"tags":[],"url":"/api/webhooks/listWebhookEndpoints"},"388":{"id":"/api/webhooks/listWebhookEndpoints-0","page_id":"/api/webhooks/listWebhookEndpoints","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/api/webhooks/listWebhookEndpoints","content":"Retrieve all configured webhook endpoints"},"389":{"id":"/api/webhooks/listWebhookEventTypes","page_id":"/api/webhooks/listWebhookEventTypes","type":"page","content":"List webhook event types","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Pulsarr API","Webhooks"],"tags":[],"url":"/api/webhooks/listWebhookEventTypes"},"390":{"id":"/api/webhooks/listWebhookEventTypes-0","page_id":"/api/webhooks/listWebhookEventTypes","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/api/webhooks/listWebhookEventTypes","content":"List all available webhook event types with descriptions"},"391":{"id":"/api/webhooks/testExistingWebhookEndpoint","page_id":"/api/webhooks/testExistingWebhookEndpoint","type":"page","content":"Test existing webhook endpoint","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Pulsarr API","Webhooks"],"tags":[],"url":"/api/webhooks/testExistingWebhookEndpoint"},"392":{"id":"/api/webhooks/testExistingWebhookEndpoint-0","page_id":"/api/webhooks/testExistingWebhookEndpoint","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/api/webhooks/testExistingWebhookEndpoint","content":"Test an existing webhook endpoint by ID"},"393":{"id":"/api/webhooks/testWebhookEndpoint","page_id":"/api/webhooks/testWebhookEndpoint","type":"page","content":"Test webhook endpoint","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Pulsarr API","Webhooks"],"tags":[],"url":"/api/webhooks/testWebhookEndpoint"},"394":{"id":"/api/webhooks/testWebhookEndpoint-0","page_id":"/api/webhooks/testWebhookEndpoint","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/api/webhooks/testWebhookEndpoint","content":"Test a webhook endpoint by sending a test payload (use before saving)"},"395":{"id":"/api/webhooks/updateWebhookEndpoint","page_id":"/api/webhooks/updateWebhookEndpoint","type":"page","content":"Update webhook endpoint","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Pulsarr API","Webhooks"],"tags":[],"url":"/api/webhooks/updateWebhookEndpoint"},"396":{"id":"/api/webhooks/updateWebhookEndpoint-0","page_id":"/api/webhooks/updateWebhookEndpoint","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/api/webhooks/updateWebhookEndpoint","content":"Update an existing webhook endpoint"},"397":{"id":"/home","page_id":"/home","type":"page","content":"Home","breadcrumbs":["Docs"],"tags":[],"url":"/home"},"398":{"id":"/home-0","page_id":"/home","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/home","content":"The dashboard you land on, with what needs your attention and how requests are flowing."},"399":{"id":"/home-1","page_id":"/home","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/home#date-range","content":"Date range"},"400":{"id":"/home-2","page_id":"/home","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/home#cards","content":"Cards"},"401":{"id":"/home-3","page_id":"/home","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/home#customize-home","content":"Customize home"},"402":{"id":"/home-4","page_id":"/home","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/home","content":"Home is the first page you see. The line under the title says whether watchlist sync is running, and the cards show what needs your attention and how requests are flowing."},"403":{"id":"/home-5","page_id":"/home","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/home#date-range","content":"The range menu, for example **Last 30 days** or **All time**, sets the period the activity cards cover."},"404":{"id":"/home-6","page_id":"/home","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/home#cards","content":"**Needs your approval** lists requests waiting in the approval queue."},"405":{"id":"/home-7","page_id":"/home","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/home#cards","content":"**Most active** shows who requests the most."},"406":{"id":"/home-8","page_id":"/home","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/home#cards","content":"**Recent requests** lists the latest requests with their status. You can filter by status and change the sort order."},"407":{"id":"/home-9","page_id":"/home","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/home#cards","content":"**Request pipeline** counts requests at each stage. **Requested** means it's in Sonarr or Radarr with no file yet. **Grabbed** means it's downloaded but nobody has been told. **Notified** means it's ready and the user was told."},"408":{"id":"/home-10","page_id":"/home","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/home#cards","content":"**Request to ready** shows how long movies and shows take to become available."},"409":{"id":"/home-11","page_id":"/home","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/home#cards","content":"**Popularity rankings** list the most watchlisted movies and shows. Select a title to see its details, where it streams, and its state in Pulsarr and in your instances."},"410":{"id":"/home-12","page_id":"/home","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/home#cards","content":"**Top genres** and **Library mix** break down what gets requested."},"411":{"id":"/home-13","page_id":"/home","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/home#cards","content":"**Placements by instance** shows where the router sent requests."},"412":{"id":"/home-14","page_id":"/home","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/home#cards","content":"**Notifications** counts what was sent, and through which channels."},"413":{"id":"/home-15","page_id":"/home","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/home#customize-home","content":"**Customize home** opens the cards as a board of rows. Drag a row by its handle to move it, or drag a card into another row. Full-width cards move with their row. **Hide** puts a card under **Hidden cards**, **Show** brings it back, and **Reset layout** restores the default. Changes apply as you make them. Select **Done** to close."},"414":{"id":"/home-16","page_id":"/home","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/home#customize-home","content":"The layout is saved in your browser, so each browser keeps its own."},"415":{"id":"/how-it-works","page_id":"/how-it-works","type":"page","content":"How Pulsarr works","breadcrumbs":["Docs"],"tags":[],"url":"/how-it-works"},"416":{"id":"/how-it-works-0","page_id":"/how-it-works","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/how-it-works","content":"What happens between someone adding a title to their Plex watchlist and being told it's ready."},"417":{"id":"/how-it-works-1","page_id":"/how-it-works","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/how-it-works#from-watchlist-to-plex","content":"From watchlist to Plex"},"418":{"id":"/how-it-works-2","page_id":"/how-it-works","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/how-it-works#how-changes-are-spotted","content":"How changes are spotted"},"419":{"id":"/how-it-works-3","page_id":"/how-it-works","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/how-it-works#users","content":"Users"},"420":{"id":"/how-it-works-4","page_id":"/how-it-works","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/how-it-works#after-the-download","content":"After the download"},"421":{"id":"/how-it-works-5","page_id":"/how-it-works","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/how-it-works","content":"Pulsarr sits between Plex watchlists and Sonarr and Radarr. Your users never use Pulsarr directly. They add titles to their watchlist in the Plex app, and Pulsarr decides what to request, where to send it, and who to tell when it's ready."},"422":{"id":"/how-it-works-6","page_id":"/how-it-works","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/how-it-works#from-watchlist-to-plex","content":"**Pulsarr spots the change,** within seconds with Plex Pass, or within about 5 minutes without it. How changes are spotted explains how."},"423":{"id":"/how-it-works-7","page_id":"/how-it-works","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/how-it-works#from-watchlist-to-plex","content":"**It filters.** A title with an exclusion isn't requested. With **Skip content already on Plex** on, nor is anything your server already has."},"424":{"id":"/how-it-works-8","page_id":"/how-it-works","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/how-it-works#from-watchlist-to-plex","content":"**It routes.** The Content router picks the Sonarr or Radarr instance, or several, and their settings. A Skip route stops the request here. With no matching route, the request goes to the default instance."},"425":{"id":"/how-it-works-9","page_id":"/how-it-works","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/how-it-works#from-watchlist-to-plex","content":"**It checks limits.** A user past their watchlist cap is skipped. Some requests need your approval first, because of a route, the user's **Require approval** setting, or their quota. Those wait in the approval queue."},"426":{"id":"/how-it-works-10","page_id":"/how-it-works","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/how-it-works#from-watchlist-to-plex","content":"**It sends the request** to Sonarr or Radarr, which search and download as usual."},"427":{"id":"/how-it-works-11","page_id":"/how-it-works","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/how-it-works#from-watchlist-to-plex","content":"**It notifies.** When Sonarr or Radarr finish importing, they tell Pulsarr through a webhook. Pulsarr then tells everyone who has the title on their watchlist, through their channels."},"428":{"id":"/how-it-works-12","page_id":"/how-it-works","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/how-it-works#how-changes-are-spotted","content":"When it starts, Pulsarr reads every watchlist. Yours comes from Plex's watchlist API. Your friends' come from Plex's community GraphQL API."},"429":{"id":"/how-it-works-13","page_id":"/how-it-works","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/how-it-works#how-changes-are-spotted","content":"With Plex Pass, Pulsarr then checks your two watchlist RSS feeds about every 10 seconds. Each new item says which friend added it, so Pulsarr requests it straight away."},"430":{"id":"/how-it-works-14","page_id":"/how-it-works","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/how-it-works#how-changes-are-spotted","content":"Without Plex Pass, Pulsarr asks those same APIs whether each watchlist changed, working through everyone every 5 minutes."},"431":{"id":"/how-it-works-15","page_id":"/how-it-works","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/how-it-works#how-changes-are-spotted","content":"Either way, Pulsarr reads every watchlist in full again every 2 hours. Plex's friends feed sometimes leaves out a particular friend's items, and the full read picks them up."},"432":{"id":"/how-it-works-16","page_id":"/how-it-works","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/how-it-works#users","content":"Pulsarr reads your own watchlist and those of your Plex friends. It adds friends as users by itself, the first time it sees them, with your new user defaults. People with access to your server who aren't friends yet show on Plex users, where you can send them a friend request."},"433":{"id":"/how-it-works-17","page_id":"/how-it-works","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/how-it-works#after-the-download","content":"A few features keep working once content is in your library:"},"434":{"id":"/how-it-works-18","page_id":"/how-it-works","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/how-it-works#after-the-download","content":"Session monitoring watches what people play, and requests the next season before they reach it."},"435":{"id":"/how-it-works-19","page_id":"/how-it-works","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/how-it-works#after-the-download","content":"User tags and Plex labels mark content with who asked for it."},"436":{"id":"/how-it-works-20","page_id":"/how-it-works","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/how-it-works#after-the-download","content":"Delete sync removes content once nobody has it on their watchlist anymore."},"437":{"id":"/","page_id":"/","type":"page","content":"Welcome to Pulsarr","breadcrumbs":["Docs"],"tags":[],"url":"/"},"438":{"id":"/-0","page_id":"/","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/","content":"Pulsarr turns Plex watchlists into Sonarr and Radarr requests."},"439":{"id":"/-1","page_id":"/","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/#introduction","content":"Introduction"},"440":{"id":"/-2","page_id":"/","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/#first-time","content":"First time?"},"441":{"id":"/-3","page_id":"/","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/#getting-help","content":"Getting help"},"442":{"id":"/-4","page_id":"/","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/#introduction","content":"Pulsarr watches your Plex watchlist and the watchlists of your Plex friends. When a movie or show is added, Pulsarr sends it to Radarr or Sonarr. When it's available, Pulsarr can notify the person who added it through Discord, Plex mobile push, Apprise or webhooks. Your users request content from the Plex app they already use, with no extra account."},"443":{"id":"/-5","page_id":"/","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/#introduction","content":"Pulsarr can only read the watchlist of someone who is a friend of your Plex account. People with access to your server who aren't friends yet show up under **Not yet friends** on the **Plex users** page, where you can send them a friend request."},"444":{"id":"/-6","page_id":"/","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/#introduction","content":"With Plex Pass, watchlist changes arrive within seconds. Without it, Pulsarr checks each watchlist on a schedule."},"445":{"id":"/-7","page_id":"/","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/#introduction","content":"The Content router decides which Sonarr or Radarr instance each title goes to, with which quality profile and root folder. Approvals and quotas let you control what gets added."},"446":{"id":"/-8","page_id":"/","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/#introduction","content":"Pulsarr runs in Docker or as a native install on Linux, macOS and Windows, and stores its data in SQLite or PostgreSQL."},"447":{"id":"/-9","page_id":"/","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/#first-time","content":"<Card title=\"How Pulsarr works\" href=\"/how-it-works\" description=\"What happens between a watchlist add and the notification that it's ready.\" />"},"448":{"id":"/-10","page_id":"/","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/#first-time","content":"<Card title=\"Quick start\" href=\"/installation/quick-start\" description=\"From installing Pulsarr to your first watchlist item reaching Sonarr or Radarr.\" />"},"449":{"id":"/-11","page_id":"/","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/#first-time","content":"<Card title=\"Installation\" href=\"/installation\" description=\"Docker and the native installers for Linux, macOS and Windows, plus the Unraid and TrueNAS app catal…\" />"},"450":{"id":"/-12","page_id":"/","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/#getting-help","content":"If you need help, ask in our Discord."},"451":{"id":"/-13","page_id":"/","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/#getting-help","content":"Only use the issue tracker if you've found a bug or have a specific feature request."},"452":{"id":"/-14","page_id":"/","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/#getting-help","content":"These docs are maintained on GitHub. To suggest an improvement, open an issue or pull request."},"453":{"id":"/installation/docker","page_id":"/installation/docker","type":"page","content":"Docker","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Installation"],"tags":[],"url":"/installation/docker"},"454":{"id":"/installation/docker-0","page_id":"/installation/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/installation/docker","content":"Run Pulsarr in Docker with Compose or docker run, and keep it updated."},"455":{"id":"/installation/docker-1","page_id":"/installation/docker","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/installation/docker#docker-compose","content":"Docker Compose"},"456":{"id":"/installation/docker-2","page_id":"/installation/docker","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/installation/docker#docker-run","content":"docker run"},"457":{"id":"/installation/docker-3","page_id":"/installation/docker","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/installation/docker#image-tags","content":"Image tags"},"458":{"id":"/installation/docker-4","page_id":"/installation/docker","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/installation/docker#synology-and-older-kernels","content":"Synology and older kernels"},"459":{"id":"/installation/docker-5","page_id":"/installation/docker","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/installation/docker#file-ownership","content":"File ownership"},"460":{"id":"/installation/docker-6","page_id":"/installation/docker","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/installation/docker#ports","content":"Ports"},"461":{"id":"/installation/docker-7","page_id":"/installation/docker","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/installation/docker#updating","content":"Updating"},"462":{"id":"/installation/docker-8","page_id":"/installation/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/installation/docker","content":"The Pulsarr image, `lakker/pulsarr`, is built for `linux/amd64` and `linux/arm64`. If this is your first install, the quick start walks through the same steps and then first-run setup."},"463":{"id":"/installation/docker-9","page_id":"/installation/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/installation/docker#docker-compose","content":"Create a folder for Pulsarr with a `.env` file and a `docker-compose.yml`."},"464":{"id":"/installation/docker-10","page_id":"/installation/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/installation/docker#docker-compose","content":"`.env` holds your time zone and any other Pulsarr environment variables:"},"465":{"id":"/installation/docker-11","page_id":"/installation/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/installation/docker#docker-compose","content":"`docker-compose.yml`:"},"466":{"id":"/installation/docker-12","page_id":"/installation/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/installation/docker#docker-compose","content":"Start it:"},"467":{"id":"/installation/docker-13","page_id":"/installation/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/installation/docker#docker-compose","content":"Then open `http://<your-server>:3003`. Pulsarr keeps its database and logs in `./data`."},"468":{"id":"/installation/docker-14","page_id":"/installation/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/installation/docker#docker-run","content":"The same container without Compose, run from the folder with your `.env`:"},"469":{"id":"/installation/docker-15","page_id":"/installation/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/installation/docker#image-tags","content":"`latest` is the newest release."},"470":{"id":"/installation/docker-16","page_id":"/installation/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/installation/docker#image-tags","content":"`beta` is the newest pre-release."},"471":{"id":"/installation/docker-17","page_id":"/installation/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/installation/docker#image-tags","content":"`0.20.0` pins an exact version, and `0.20` follows the newest patch of that minor version."},"472":{"id":"/installation/docker-18","page_id":"/installation/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/installation/docker#image-tags","content":"`node`, `beta-node`, `0.20.0-node` and `0.20-node` are the same tags for the Node.js image."},"473":{"id":"/installation/docker-19","page_id":"/installation/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/installation/docker#synology-and-older-kernels","content":"On a Synology NAS, or any host with a Linux kernel older than 4.11, use the Node.js image, `lakker/pulsarr:node`. The default image needs a newer kernel. Both images run the same app."},"474":{"id":"/installation/docker-20","page_id":"/installation/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/installation/docker#file-ownership","content":"Pulsarr runs as the user and group set by `PUID` and `PGID`, which both default to `1000`. On start it takes ownership of anything in `./data` that has a different owner. Set them to your user on the host, which `id -u` and `id -g` print."},"475":{"id":"/installation/docker-21","page_id":"/installation/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/installation/docker#file-ownership","content":"If you run the container with Compose's `user:` option instead, Pulsarr skips the ownership change. `./data` must then already be writable by that user, or the container stops with an error."},"476":{"id":"/installation/docker-22","page_id":"/installation/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/installation/docker#ports","content":"To serve Pulsarr on another port, change the left side of the mapping, for example `\"8080:3003\"`. Sonarr and Radarr still need to reach Pulsarr for webhooks. If they can't, the connection test in Pulsarr offers **Fix the address**, where you set the address and port they should use."},"477":{"id":"/installation/docker-23","page_id":"/installation/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/installation/docker#updating","content":"Pull the new image and recreate the container:"},"478":{"id":"/installation/docker-24","page_id":"/installation/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/installation/docker#updating","content":"Pulsarr updates its database on start, so there's nothing else to run."},"479":{"id":"/installation/environment-variables","page_id":"/installation/environment-variables","type":"page","content":"Environment variables","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Installation"],"tags":[],"url":"/installation/environment-variables"},"480":{"id":"/installation/environment-variables-0","page_id":"/installation/environment-variables","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/installation/environment-variables","content":"Every setting Pulsarr reads from .env, with its default."},"481":{"id":"/installation/environment-variables-1","page_id":"/installation/environment-variables","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/installation/environment-variables#server","content":"Server"},"482":{"id":"/installation/environment-variables-2","page_id":"/installation/environment-variables","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/installation/environment-variables#database","content":"Database"},"483":{"id":"/installation/environment-variables-3","page_id":"/installation/environment-variables","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/installation/environment-variables#security","content":"Security"},"484":{"id":"/installation/environment-variables-4","page_id":"/installation/environment-variables","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/installation/environment-variables#plex","content":"Plex"},"485":{"id":"/installation/environment-variables-5","page_id":"/installation/environment-variables","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/installation/environment-variables#sonarr-and-radarr","content":"Sonarr and Radarr"},"486":{"id":"/installation/environment-variables-6","page_id":"/installation/environment-variables","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/installation/environment-variables#tmdb","content":"TMDB"},"487":{"id":"/installation/environment-variables-7","page_id":"/installation/environment-variables","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/installation/environment-variables#notifications","content":"Notifications"},"488":{"id":"/installation/environment-variables-8","page_id":"/installation/environment-variables","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/installation/environment-variables#user-tags","content":"User tags"},"489":{"id":"/installation/environment-variables-9","page_id":"/installation/environment-variables","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/installation/environment-variables#delete-sync","content":"Delete sync"},"490":{"id":"/installation/environment-variables-10","page_id":"/installation/environment-variables","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/installation/environment-variables#maintainerr","content":"Maintainerr"},"491":{"id":"/installation/environment-variables-11","page_id":"/installation/environment-variables","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/installation/environment-variables#new-user-defaults","content":"New user defaults"},"492":{"id":"/installation/environment-variables-12","page_id":"/installation/environment-variables","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/installation/environment-variables#json-settings","content":"JSON settings"},"493":{"id":"/installation/environment-variables-13","page_id":"/installation/environment-variables","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/installation/environment-variables","content":"Pulsarr reads these from `.env`, or from the container's environment in Docker. Most of them are also settings in the app, and you only need `.env` to fix a value before first start or to keep it under version control."},"494":{"id":"/installation/environment-variables-14","page_id":"/installation/environment-variables","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/installation/environment-variables","content":"A variable in `.env` replaces the value saved in the app every time Pulsarr starts. This happens even when the variable is set to an empty value. A change you make in the app lasts only until the next restart, so remove the variable from `.env` if you want to manage that setting in the app."},"495":{"id":"/installation/environment-variables-15","page_id":"/installation/environment-variables","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/installation/environment-variables","content":"Restart Pulsarr after changing `.env`. Values marked JSON take one line of JSON, for example `sonarrTags=[\"4k\",\"kids\"]`."},"496":{"id":"/installation/environment-variables-16","page_id":"/installation/environment-variables","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/installation/environment-variables#server","content":"| Variable | Default | Description                                                                  |\n| -------- | ------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `TZ`     |         | Time zone for the container, for example `America/Los_Angeles`. Docker only. |","table":"table-0"},"497":{"id":"/installation/environment-variables-17","page_id":"/installation/environment-variables","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/installation/environment-variables#server","content":"| Variable     | Default | Description              |\n| ------------ | ------- | ------------------------ |\n| `listenPort` | `3003`  | Port Pulsarr listens on. |","table":"table-0"},"498":{"id":"/installation/environment-variables-18","page_id":"/installation/environment-variables","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/installation/environment-variables#server","content":"| Variable  | Default            | Description                                              