/installation/environment-variables-121","page_id":"/installation/environment-variables","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/installation/environment-variables#json-settings","content":"`plexLabelSync`, from the **Plex labels** page:"},"602":{"id":"/installation/environment-variables-122","page_id":"/installation/environment-variables","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/installation/environment-variables#json-settings","content":"`plexSessionMonitoring`, from the **Session monitoring** page:"},"603":{"id":"/installation","page_id":"/installation","type":"page","content":"Installation","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Installation"],"tags":[],"url":"/installation"},"604":{"id":"/installation-0","page_id":"/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/installation","content":"Install Pulsarr with Docker or the native installers, or find it in the Unraid and TrueNAS app catalogs."},"605":{"id":"/installation-1","page_id":"/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/installation","content":"New to Pulsarr? Start with the quick start. It goes from install to your first watchlist item reaching Sonarr or Radarr."},"606":{"id":"/installation-2","page_id":"/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/installation","content":"<Card title=\"Quick start\" href=\"/installation/quick-start\" description=\"Install with Docker and run first-run setup.\" />"},"607":{"id":"/installation-3","page_id":"/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/installation","content":"<Card title=\"Docker\" href=\"/installation/docker\" description=\"Compose, docker run, image tags, file ownership and updates.\" />"},"608":{"id":"/installation-4","page_id":"/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/installation","content":"<Card title=\"Native installers\" href=\"/installation/native\" description=\"Linux, Windows and macOS builds that need no Docker.\" />"},"609":{"id":"/installation-5","page_id":"/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/installation","content":"<Card title=\"PostgreSQL\" href=\"/installation/postgresql\" description=\"Use PostgreSQL instead of SQLite, or move an existing install.\" />"},"610":{"id":"/installation-6","page_id":"/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/installation","content":"<Card title=\"Environment variables\" href=\"/installation/environment-variables\" description=\"Every setting Pulsarr reads from .env, with its default.\" />"},"611":{"id":"/installation-7","page_id":"/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/installation","content":"Pulsarr is also in the Unraid Community Applications and TrueNAS community app catalogs. Search for Pulsarr in either one."},"612":{"id":"/installation-8","page_id":"/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/installation","content":"For hosted Pulsarr, ElfHosted runs it for you."},"613":{"id":"/installation/native","page_id":"/installation/native","type":"page","content":"Native installers","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Installation"],"tags":[],"url":"/installation/native"},"614":{"id":"/installation/native-0","page_id":"/installation/native","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/installation/native","content":"Install Pulsarr on Linux, Windows or macOS without Docker."},"615":{"id":"/installation/native-1","page_id":"/installation/native","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/installation/native#linux","content":"Linux"},"616":{"id":"/installation/native-2","page_id":"/installation/native","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/installation/native#windows","content":"Windows"},"617":{"id":"/installation/native-3","page_id":"/installation/native","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/installation/native#macos","content":"macOS"},"618":{"id":"/installation/native-4","page_id":"/installation/native","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/installation/native#start-on-login","content":"Start on login"},"619":{"id":"/installation/native-5","page_id":"/installation/native","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/installation/native#portable-zips","content":"Portable zips"},"620":{"id":"/installation/native-6","page_id":"/installation/native","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/installation/native#settings-in-env","content":"Settings in .env"},"621":{"id":"/installation/native-7","page_id":"/installation/native","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/installation/native","content":"Each release includes builds for Linux, Windows and macOS with the runtime included, so there's nothing else to install. Download them from the latest release. After installing, open `http://<your-server>:3003`, or `http://localhost:3003` on the same machine, and continue with Create the admin account in the quick start."},"622":{"id":"/installation/native-8","page_id":"/installation/native","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/installation/native#linux","content":"The install script needs `curl`, `unzip` and systemd, and supports x64 and arm64:"},"623":{"id":"/installation/native-9","page_id":"/installation/native","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/installation/native#linux","content":"It installs the latest release to `/opt/pulsarr`, creates a `pulsarr` system user, and starts Pulsarr as a systemd service. On systems without systemd, use Docker instead."},"624":{"id":"/installation/native-10","page_id":"/installation/native","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/installation/native#linux","content":"Manage the service with `systemctl`:"},"625":{"id":"/installation/native-11","page_id":"/installation/native","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/installation/native#linux","content":"To update, run the install script again. It keeps your `.env` and data."},"626":{"id":"/installation/native-12","page_id":"/installation/native","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/installation/native#linux","content":"To uninstall, add `--uninstall` to keep your data, or `--purge` to delete it:"},"627":{"id":"/installation/native-13","page_id":"/installation/native","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/installation/native#linux","content":"Where files live:"},"628":{"id":"/installation/native-14","page_id":"/installation/native","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/installation/native#linux","content":"`/opt/pulsarr/.env`"},"629":{"id":"/installation/native-15","page_id":"/installation/native","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/installation/native#linux","content":"`/opt/pulsarr/data/db/`"},"630":{"id":"/installation/native-16","page_id":"/installation/native","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/installation/native#linux","content":"`/opt/pulsarr/data/logs/`"},"631":{"id":"/installation/native-17","page_id":"/installation/native","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/installation/native#windows","content":"Download and run `pulsarr-vX.Y.Z-windows-x64-setup.exe`. The installer isn't code-signed, so Windows SmartScreen may warn you. Select **More info**, then **Run anyway**."},"632":{"id":"/installation/native-18","page_id":"/installation/native","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/installation/native#windows","content":"The **Full installation** runs Pulsarr as a Windows service, so it starts without anyone logging in. **Compact installation** skips the service and you start Pulsarr yourself. The installer also adds a Windows Firewall rule by default, so other devices on your network can reach Pulsarr. Sonarr and Radarr on another machine need it to send webhooks."},"633":{"id":"/installation/native-19","page_id":"/installation/native","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/installation/native#windows","content":"Manage the service in `services.msc`, or from an administrator prompt:"},"634":{"id":"/installation/native-20","page_id":"/installation/native","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/installation/native#windows","content":"To update, run the new installer. It stops the service, replaces the program files and keeps your settings and data."},"635":{"id":"/installation/native-21","page_id":"/installation/native","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/installation/native#windows","content":"To uninstall, use **Add or remove programs**. The uninstaller asks whether to delete your data as well."},"636":{"id":"/installation/native-22","page_id":"/installation/native","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/installation/native#windows","content":"Pulsarr installs to `C:\\Program Files\\Pulsarr`. Where files live:"},"637":{"id":"/installation/native-23","page_id":"/installation/native","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/installation/native#windows","content":"`C:\\ProgramData\\Pulsarr\\.env`"},"638":{"id":"/installation/native-24","page_id":"/installation/native","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/installation/native#windows","content":"`C:\\ProgramData\\Pulsarr\\db\\`"},"639":{"id":"/installation/native-25","page_id":"/installation/native","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/installation/native#windows","content":"`C:\\ProgramData\\Pulsarr\\logs\\`"},"640":{"id":"/installation/native-26","page_id":"/installation/native","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/installation/native#macos","content":"macOS 13 (Ventura) or later is required."},"641":{"id":"/installation/native-27","page_id":"/installation/native","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/installation/native#macos","content":"Download `pulsarr-vX.Y.Z-macos-arm64.dmg` for Apple silicon, or `pulsarr-vX.Y.Z-macos-x64.dmg` for Intel."},"642":{"id":"/installation/native-28","page_id":"/installation/native","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/installation/native#macos","content":"Open the DMG and drag **Pulsarr** to **Applications**."},"643":{"id":"/installation/native-29","page_id":"/installation/native","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/installation/native#macos","content":"The app isn't signed, so remove the quarantine flag macOS adds to downloads:"},"644":{"id":"/installation/native-30","page_id":"/installation/native","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/installation/native#macos","content":"Open Pulsarr. It runs in the background, with no window or Dock icon."},"645":{"id":"/installation/native-31","page_id":"/installation/native","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/installation/native#macos","content":"To stop Pulsarr, run `pkill -f Pulsarr.app`."},"646":{"id":"/installation/native-32","page_id":"/installation/native","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/installation/native#macos","content":"To update, stop Pulsarr, drag the new version over the old one, and run the `xattr` command again."},"647":{"id":"/installation/native-33","page_id":"/installation/native","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/installation/native#macos","content":"Where files live:"},"648":{"id":"/installation/native-34","page_id":"/installation/native","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/installation/native#macos","content":"`~/.config/Pulsarr/.env`, created from a template the first time Pulsarr starts"},"649":{"id":"/installation/native-35","page_id":"/installation/native","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/installation/native#macos","content":"`~/.config/Pulsarr/db/`"},"650":{"id":"/installation/native-36","page_id":"/installation/native","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/installation/native#macos","content":"`~/.config/Pulsarr/logs/`"},"651":{"id":"/installation/native-37","page_id":"/installation/native","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/installation/native#start-on-login","content":"To start Pulsarr when you log in, add a LaunchAgent:"},"652":{"id":"/installation/native-38","page_id":"/installation/native","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/installation/native#start-on-login","content":"`KeepAlive` restarts Pulsarr if it stops, so stop it with `launchctl unload ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.pulsarr.plist` instead of `pkill`."},"653":{"id":"/installation/native-39","page_id":"/installation/native","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/installation/native#portable-zips","content":"Each platform also has a plain zip, such as `pulsarr-vX.Y.Z-linux-x64.zip`. Extract it anywhere and run `./start.sh`, or `start.bat` on Windows. On macOS, remove the quarantine flag first, as the zip's `README.txt` explains. To update, stop Pulsarr, then run `./update.sh` or `update.bat` with the path to the new zip. Each zip has a `README.txt` that covers running it as a service."},"654":{"id":"/installation/native-40","page_id":"/installation/native","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/installation/native#settings-in-env","content":"Almost every setting can also be set in `.env`. See environment variables for the full list. The installers and the macOS app create it for you, at the paths listed above. Restart Pulsarr after changing it."},"655":{"id":"/installation/postgresql","page_id":"/installation/postgresql","type":"page","content":"PostgreSQL","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Installation"],"tags":[],"url":"/installation/postgresql"},"656":{"id":"/installation/postgresql-0","page_id":"/installation/postgresql","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/installation/postgresql","content":"Run Pulsarr on PostgreSQL instead of SQLite, from the start or by moving an existing install."},"657":{"id":"/installation/postgresql-1","page_id":"/installation/postgresql","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/installation/postgresql#start-on-postgresql","content":"Start on PostgreSQL"},"658":{"id":"/installation/postgresql-2","page_id":"/installation/postgresql","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/installation/postgresql#move-from-sqlite","content":"Move from SQLite"},"659":{"id":"/installation/postgresql-3","page_id":"/installation/postgresql","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/installation/postgresql#go-back-to-sqlite","content":"Go back to SQLite"},"660":{"id":"/installation/postgresql-4","page_id":"/installation/postgresql","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/installation/postgresql","content":"Pulsarr uses SQLite by default and needs no setup for it. You can use PostgreSQL instead, either from the first start or by moving an existing SQLite install across."},"661":{"id":"/installation/postgresql-5","page_id":"/installation/postgresql","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/installation/postgresql","content":"Pulsarr creates the tables, but not the database. Create an empty database and give your user full rights on it first:"},"662":{"id":"/installation/postgresql-6","page_id":"/installation/postgresql","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/installation/postgresql#start-on-postgresql","content":"Add the connection to `.env` before Pulsarr starts for the first time:"},"663":{"id":"/installation/postgresql-7","page_id":"/installation/postgresql","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/installation/postgresql#start-on-postgresql","content":"Or give the whole connection as `dbConnectionString=postgresql://user:password@host:5432/pulsarr`, which is used instead of the separate settings. Pulsarr sets up the tables when it starts."},"664":{"id":"/installation/postgresql-8","page_id":"/installation/postgresql","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/installation/postgresql#move-from-sqlite","content":"These steps use Docker and the `docker-compose.migration.yml` from the repository. Put it next to your `docker-compose.yml`."},"665":{"id":"/installation/postgresql-9","page_id":"/installation/postgresql","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/installation/postgresql#move-from-sqlite","content":"Stop Pulsarr with `docker compose down`."},"666":{"id":"/installation/postgresql-10","page_id":"/installation/postgresql","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/installation/postgresql#move-from-sqlite","content":"Bring the SQLite database up to date, with `.env` still set to SQLite:"},"667":{"id":"/installation/postgresql-11","page_id":"/installation/postgresql","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/installation/postgresql#move-from-sqlite","content":"Add the PostgreSQL settings above to `.env`."},"668":{"id":"/installation/postgresql-12","page_id":"/installation/postgresql","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/installation/postgresql#move-from-sqlite","content":"Create the tables in PostgreSQL:"},"669":{"id":"/installation/postgresql-13","page_id":"/installation/postgresql","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/installation/postgresql#move-from-sqlite","content":"Copy the data across. It asks you to confirm before it starts:"},"670":{"id":"/installation/postgresql-14","page_id":"/installation/postgresql","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/installation/postgresql#move-from-sqlite","content":"It checks both connections, backs up the SQLite database to `./data/backups/`, copies every table and checks that the row counts match."},"671":{"id":"/installation/postgresql-15","page_id":"/installation/postgresql","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/installation/postgresql#move-from-sqlite","content":"Start Pulsarr with `docker compose up -d`."},"672":{"id":"/installation/postgresql-16","page_id":"/installation/postgresql","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/installation/postgresql#move-from-sqlite","content":"To see progress for each batch, run the copy step with the script's full command and `--verbose`. `--help` lists the other options."},"673":{"id":"/installation/postgresql-17","page_id":"/installation/postgresql","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/installation/postgresql#go-back-to-sqlite","content":"Stop Pulsarr, remove the PostgreSQL settings from `.env` so `dbType` is back to `sqlite`, and start it again. Your SQLite database is still in `./data/db/`, and the copy made before the move is in `./data/backups/`."},"674":{"id":"/installation/quick-start","page_id":"/installation/quick-start","type":"page","content":"Quick start","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Installation"],"tags":[],"url":"/installation/quick-start"},"675":{"id":"/installation/quick-start-0","page_id":"/installation/quick-start","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/installation/quick-start","content":"Install Pulsarr with Docker and get your first watchlist item into Sonarr or Radarr."},"676":{"id":"/installation/quick-start-1","page_id":"/installation/quick-start","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/installation/quick-start#before-you-start","content":"Before you start"},"677":{"id":"/installation/quick-start-2","page_id":"/installation/quick-start","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/installation/quick-start#install-pulsarr","content":"Install Pulsarr"},"678":{"id":"/installation/quick-start-3","page_id":"/installation/quick-start","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/installation/quick-start#create-the-admin-account","content":"Create the admin account"},"679":{"id":"/installation/quick-start-4","page_id":"/installation/quick-start","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/installation/quick-start#run-setup","content":"Run setup"},"680":{"id":"/installation/quick-start-5","page_id":"/installation/quick-start","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/installation/quick-start#check-that-it-works","content":"Check that it works"},"681":{"id":"/installation/quick-start-6","page_id":"/installation/quick-start","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/installation/quick-start","content":"This guide installs Pulsarr with Docker Compose and walks through first-run setup. At the end, a title you add to your Plex watchlist shows up in Sonarr or Radarr."},"682":{"id":"/installation/quick-start-7","page_id":"/installation/quick-start","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/installation/quick-start#before-you-start","content":"You need:"},"683":{"id":"/installation/quick-start-8","page_id":"/installation/quick-start","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/installation/quick-start#before-you-start","content":"Docker with Docker Compose. To install without Docker, see Native installers."},"684":{"id":"/installation/quick-start-9","page_id":"/installation/quick-start","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/installation/quick-start#before-you-start","content":"The Plex account that owns your Plex server."},"685":{"id":"/installation/quick-start-10","page_id":"/installation/quick-start","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/installation/quick-start#before-you-start","content":"Sonarr and Radarr, with the API key from each. You'll find it in Settings > General."},"686":{"id":"/installation/quick-start-11","page_id":"/installation/quick-start","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/installation/quick-start#before-you-start","content":"Pulsarr reads your own watchlist and the watchlists of your Plex friends. Anyone who isn't a friend of your Plex account is skipped."},"687":{"id":"/installation/quick-start-12","page_id":"/installation/quick-start","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/installation/quick-start#before-you-start","content":"Each friend also decides who can see their watchlist, in their own Plex privacy settings. If it's set to Private, Pulsarr can't see it, and Plex doesn't say so. It looks the same as an empty watchlist. They can change it from the privacy icon next to Watchlist on their Plex profile, or in the Plex web app under Settings > Account > Account Visibility & Activity Sharing."},"688":{"id":"/installation/quick-start-13","page_id":"/installation/quick-start","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/installation/quick-start#install-pulsarr","content":"Create a folder for Pulsarr. In it, add a `.env` file with your time zone:"},"689":{"id":"/installation/quick-start-14","page_id":"/installation/quick-start","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/installation/quick-start#install-pulsarr","content":"Almost every Pulsarr setting can also be set in `.env`, as listed in environment variables. For this guide, the time zone is all you need."},"690":{"id":"/installation/quick-start-15","page_id":"/installation/quick-start","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/installation/quick-start#install-pulsarr","content":"Add a `docker-compose.yml` next to it:"},"691":{"id":"/installation/quick-start-16","page_id":"/installation/quick-start","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/installation/quick-start#install-pulsarr","content":"Pulsarr keeps its database and logs in `./data`."},"692":{"id":"/installation/quick-start-17","page_id":"/installation/quick-start","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/installation/quick-start#install-pulsarr","content":"Start it:"},"693":{"id":"/installation/quick-start-18","page_id":"/installation/quick-start","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/installation/quick-start#create-the-admin-account","content":"Open `http://<your-server>:3003`. On first visit Pulsarr asks you to create the admin account. Fill in **Email**, **Username**, **Password** and **Confirm password**, then select **Create account**. Sign in with the new account."},"694":{"id":"/installation/quick-start-19","page_id":"/installation/quick-start","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/installation/quick-start#run-setup","content":"After you sign in, the setup dialog opens. It has six steps. The other steps stay locked until you link a Plex account."},"695":{"id":"/installation/quick-start-20","page_id":"/installation/quick-start","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/installation/quick-start#run-setup","content":"**Plex account.** Select **Sign in with Plex**, then **Open plex.tv/link** and approve the code. If you'd rather paste a Plex token, use **Paste a token**."},"696":{"id":"/installation/quick-start-21","page_id":"/installation/quick-start","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/installation/quick-start#run-setup","content":"**Plex server.** The connection starts on **Automatic**, which lets Pulsarr pick the best connection. Select **Test connection** to check it, then **Continue**. Choose **Address** only if you want to enter the server address yourself."},"697":{"id":"/installation/quick-start-22","page_id":"/installation/quick-start","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/installation/quick-start#run-setup","content":"**Sonarr.** Enter a **Name**, the **URL** and the **API key**, then select **Test connection**. Once it connects, pick a **Quality profile** and **Root folder** and select **Save and continue**."},"698":{"id":"/installation/quick-start-23","page_id":"/installation/quick-start","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/installation/quick-start#run-setup","content":"The test also checks that Sonarr can reach Pulsarr, which it needs to report finished downloads. If it says Sonarr can't reach Pulsarr, select **Fix the address**. Choose how your servers reach Pulsarr, for example **IP address** with your server's address, then select **Save**. This is common when Sonarr runs in its own Docker container, where `localhost` means the container itself."},"699":{"id":"/installation/quick-start-24","page_id":"/installation/quick-start","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/installation/quick-start#run-setup","content":"**Radarr.** The same as Sonarr."},"700":{"id":"/installation/quick-start-25","page_id":"/installation/quick-start","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/installation/quick-start#run-setup","content":"**New user defaults.** Pulsarr adds users on its own. Each time it syncs, any Plex friend it hasn't seen before becomes a Pulsarr user with these settings. That includes everyone found by the first sync in the next step. **Sync watchlist** is on by default, so their watchlists are read. Turn on **Require approval** if you want to approve each request first, or **Limit requests** under **Movies** and **Shows** to give new users a quota."},"701":{"id":"/installation/quick-start-26","page_id":"/installation/quick-start","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/installation/quick-start#run-setup","content":"**Start syncing.** Select **Sync watchlists** to read every watchlist once. When every row shows **Done**, select **Start workflow**. Leave **Start on launch** on so syncing starts again after a restart. The dialog closes and the sidebar shows **Sync running**."},"702":{"id":"/installation/quick-start-27","page_id":"/installation/quick-start","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/installation/quick-start#run-setup","content":"The first Sonarr and the first Radarr you add become the default instances. Requests go to them until you add rules in the **Content router**."},"703":{"id":"/installation/quick-start-28","page_id":"/installation/quick-start","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/installation/quick-start#run-setup","content":"To stop or start the workflow later, select **Sync running** at the bottom of the sidebar and use **Stop** or **Start**. To open setup again, select your account at the bottom of the sidebar, then **Run setup**."},"704":{"id":"/installation/quick-start-29","page_id":"/installation/quick-start","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/installation/quick-start#check-that-it-works","content":"Add a movie to your Plex watchlist, then open Radarr. The movie shows up there once Pulsarr picks up the change. With Plex Pass that takes seconds. Without it, Pulsarr checks watchlists on a schedule."},"705":{"id":"/installation/quick-start-30","page_id":"/installation/quick-start","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/installation/quick-start#check-that-it-works","content":"If someone's watchlist isn't syncing, check their row on Plex users. It shows whether they're a Plex friend yet, and whether their watchlist is coming through."},"706":{"id":"/library/content-router","page_id":"/library/content-router","type":"page","content":"Content router","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Library"],"tags":[],"url":"/library/content-router"},"707":{"id":"/library/content-router-0","page_id":"/library/content-router","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/library/content-router","content":"Send each request to the right Sonarr or Radarr instance based on what it is and who asked for it."},"708":{"id":"/library/content-router-1","page_id":"/library/content-router","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/library/content-router#add-a-route","content":"Add a route"},"709":{"id":"/library/content-router-2","page_id":"/library/content-router","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/library/content-router#conditions","content":"Conditions"},"710":{"id":"/library/content-router-3","page_id":"/library/content-router","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/library/content-router#approval-and-quotas","content":"Approval and quotas"},"711":{"id":"/library/content-router-4","page_id":"/library/content-router","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/library/content-router#order-and-priority","content":"Order and priority"},"712":{"id":"/library/content-router-5","page_id":"/library/content-router","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/library/content-router#when-nothing-matches","content":"When nothing matches"},"713":{"id":"/library/content-router-6","page_id":"/library/content-router","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/library/content-router","content":"Without routes, every request goes to the default Sonarr or Radarr instance. Routes send matching requests somewhere else, with their own settings, or skip them. Manage them under **Library** > **Content router**, which has a **Movies** tab for Radarr routes and a **TV shows** tab for Sonarr routes."},"714":{"id":"/library/content-router-7","page_id":"/library/content-router","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/library/content-router","content":"Each route shows its conditions and where matching requests go. The switch on a route turns it on or off without deleting it."},"715":{"id":"/library/content-router-8","page_id":"/library/content-router","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/library/content-router#add-a-route","content":"Select **Add route**, or the arrow on an existing route to edit it. Give it a **Route name**, set its conditions, then choose what happens **When a request matches**:"},"716":{"id":"/library/content-router-9","page_id":"/library/content-router","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/library/content-router#add-a-route","content":"**Send to Sonarr** or **Send to Radarr** sends it to the **Instance** you pick. The route has its own quality profile, root folder, tags and other settings. Leave any of them on **Use instance default** to keep the instance's setting. Tags you list replace the instance's tags."},"717":{"id":"/library/content-router-10","page_id":"/library/content-router","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/library/content-router#add-a-route","content":"**Skip** never sends it anywhere."},"718":{"id":"/library/content-router-11","page_id":"/library/content-router","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/library/content-router#add-a-route","content":"Select **Save route** when you're done."},"719":{"id":"/library/content-router-12","page_id":"/library/content-router","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/library/content-router#conditions","content":"**Match** decides whether a request must meet **All** of the conditions or **Any** of them. Each condition is a field, an operator and a value, for example **Year** **is above** 2000. **Add condition** adds another. **Add group** adds a nested set with its own **All** or **Any**. **Not** reverses a condition or a whole group."},"720":{"id":"/library/content-router-13","page_id":"/library/content-router","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/library/content-router#conditions","content":"The route above sends a movie to Radarr Kids when it's Animation or Family, or rated G or PG, and isn't Horror."},"721":{"id":"/library/content-router-14","page_id":"/library/content-router","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/library/content-router#conditions","content":"Fields for movies and TV shows:"},"722":{"id":"/library/content-router-15","page_id":"/library/content-router","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/library/content-router#conditions","content":"**Genres**. When a condition checks for anime, Pulsarr also looks the title up in the community anime list and adds an \"anime\" genre if it's there."},"723":{"id":"/library/content-router-16","page_id":"/library/content-router","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/library/content-router#conditions","content":"**User**, the person who requested it."},"724":{"id":"/library/content-router-17","page_id":"/library/content-router","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/library/content-router#conditions","content":"**Plex list**, a custom Plex list owned by the requester."},"725":{"id":"/library/content-router-18","page_id":"/library/content-router","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/library/content-router#conditions","content":"**Year**, **Language** and **Certification**."},"726":{"id":"/library/content-router-19","page_id":"/library/content-router","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/library/content-router#conditions","content":"**Streaming services**, where the title streams in your TMDB region."},"727":{"id":"/library/content-router-20","page_id":"/library/content-router","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/library/content-router#conditions","content":"**IMDb rating**, with an optional **Minimum votes**, **RT critic score**, **RT audience score** and **TMDB rating**."},"728":{"id":"/library/content-router-21","page_id":"/library/content-router","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/library/content-router#conditions","content":"TV shows also have **Season** and **Series status**. Movies also have **Movie status**."},"729":{"id":"/library/content-router-22","page_id":"/library/content-router","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/library/content-router#approval-and-quotas","content":"A route can also change how matching requests are approved:"},"730":{"id":"/library/content-router-23","page_id":"/library/content-router","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/library/content-router#approval-and-quotas","content":"**Always require approval** holds matching requests in the approval queue, even from users who can request freely. **Approval reason** is shown to admins on the held request."},"731":{"id":"/library/content-router-24","page_id":"/library/content-router","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/library/content-router#approval-and-quotas","content":"**Bypass user quotas** means matching requests don't count toward the requester's quota."},"732":{"id":"/library/content-router-25","page_id":"/library/content-router","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/library/content-router#order-and-priority","content":"Every matching route runs, so one request can go to several instances. When two matching routes send to the same instance, the one nearer the top wins. The top matching route also decides approval and quota bypass. Routes lower down add neither."},"733":{"id":"/library/content-router-26","page_id":"/library/content-router","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/library/content-router#order-and-priority","content":"**Skip** routes always run first. A matching Skip route stops the request from going anywhere, whatever the other routes say."},"734":{"id":"/library/content-router-27","page_id":"/library/content-router","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/library/content-router#order-and-priority","content":"To change the order, select **Reorder**, drag the routes into place and select **Save order**. Skip routes stay pinned under **Always first**."},"735":{"id":"/library/content-router-28","page_id":"/library/content-router","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/library/content-router#when-nothing-matches","content":"A request no route sends anywhere goes to the default instance, as the note at the bottom of the list says. To skip it instead, turn on **Skip content no route matches** on the default instance under Sonarr and Radarr. Movies and TV shows are set separately."},"736":{"id":"/library/delete-sync","page_id":"/library/delete-sync","type":"page","content":"Delete sync","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Library"],"tags":[],"url":"/library/delete-sync"},"737":{"id":"/library/delete-sync-0","page_id":"/library/delete-sync","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/library/delete-sync","content":"Remove movies and shows from Sonarr and Radarr once nobody wants them."},"738":{"id":"/library/delete-sync-1","page_id":"/library/delete-sync","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/library/delete-sync#mode","content":"Mode"},"739":{"id":"/library/delete-sync-2","page_id":"/library/delete-sync","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/library/delete-sync#what-may-be-deleted","content":"What may be deleted"},"740":{"id":"/library/delete-sync-3","page_id":"/library/delete-sync","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/library/delete-sync#what-protects-content","content":"What protects content"},"741":{"id":"/library/delete-sync-4","page_id":"/library/delete-sync","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/library/delete-sync#runs-and-schedule","content":"Runs and schedule"},"742":{"id":"/library/delete-sync-5","page_id":"/library/delete-sync","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/library/delete-sync#notifications","content":"Notifications"},"743":{"id":"/library/delete-sync-6","page_id":"/library/delete-sync","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/library/delete-sync","content":"Delete sync removes content from Sonarr and Radarr when nobody wants it anymore. Set it up under **Library** > **Delete sync**. It deletes nothing until you run it or turn on its schedule, and a dry run shows what it would delete first."},"744":{"id":"/library/delete-sync-7","page_id":"/library/delete-sync","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/library/delete-sync#mode","content":"**Decide by** sets what counts as no longer wanted:"},"745":{"id":"/library/delete-sync-8","page_id":"/library/delete-sync","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/library/delete-sync#mode","content":"**Watchlist based** deletes anything that isn't on any counted user's watchlist. With **Respect user sync settings** on, only the watchlists of users with sync on count."},"746":{"id":"/library/delete-sync-9","page_id":"/library/delete-sync","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/library/delete-sync#mode","content":"**Tag based** deletes anything carrying the **Removal tag**, which comes from User tags. Matching ignores case. **Required tag pattern** is an optional regular expression, and when set, content also needs a tag that matches it."},"747":{"id":"/library/delete-sync-10","page_id":"/library/delete-sync","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/library/delete-sync#mode","content":"Either way, a title excluded for all its watchlisters, or for everyone, counts as unwanted. In tag based mode it doesn't need the removal tag."},"748":{"id":"/library/delete-sync-11","page_id":"/library/delete-sync","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/library/delete-sync#what-may-be-deleted","content":"Nothing outside these choices is deleted:"},"749":{"id":"/library/delete-sync-12","page_id":"/library/delete-sync","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/library/delete-sync#what-may-be-deleted","content":"**Delete movies** removes movies from Radarr."},"750":{"id":"/library/delete-sync-13","page_id":"/library/delete-sync","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/library/delete-sync#what-may-be-deleted","content":"**Delete ended shows** removes shows Sonarr marks as ended."},"751":{"id":"/library/delete-sync-14","page_id":"/library/delete-sync","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/library/delete-sync#what-may-be-deleted","content":"**Delete continuing shows** removes every other show."},"752":{"id":"/library/delete-sync-15","page_id":"/library/delete-sync","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/library/delete-sync#what-may-be-deleted","content":"**Delete files** also deletes the media files from disk."},"753":{"id":"/library/delete-sync-16","page_id":"/library/delete-sync","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/library/delete-sync#what-may-be-deleted","content":"**Tracked content only** limits deletion to content requested through Pulsarr."},"754":{"id":"/library/delete-sync-17","page_id":"/library/delete-sync","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/library/delete-sync#what-may-be-deleted","content":"**Clean up approval records** removes approval records for deleted content."},"755":{"id":"/library/delete-sync-18","page_id":"/library/delete-sync","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/library/delete-sync#what-protects-content","content":"Anything a guard covers is skipped:"},"756":{"id":"/library/delete-sync-19","page_id":"/library/delete-sync","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/library/delete-sync#what-protects-content","content":"**Playlist protection** skips anything in a Plex playlist with the **Playlist name**, in any user's account. Each run creates the playlist for users who don't have it yet."},"757":{"id":"/library/delete-sync-20","page_id":"/library/delete-sync","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/library/delete-sync#what-protects-content","content":"**Max deletion** aborts a run that would delete more than this percentage of your library."},"758":{"id":"/library/delete-sync-21","page_id":"/library/delete-sync","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/library/delete-sync#runs-and-schedule","content":"Select **Dry run** to preview a run without deleting anything. A dry run still refreshes watchlists and sends notifications. The result shows how much it would delete of each type, and lists every title."},"759":{"id":"/library/delete-sync-22","page_id":"/library/delete-sync","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/library/delete-sync#runs-and-schedule","content":"**Run now** runs once with the saved settings. **Run on a schedule** runs it at the **Day and time** you choose. Deleting can't be undone, so do a dry run first."},"760":{"id":"/library/delete-sync-23","page_id":"/library/delete-sync","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/library/delete-sync#notifications","content":"**Send the run summary to** picks where each run's summary goes, dry runs included. **Only when something was deleted** skips the summary when a run deletes nothing."},"761":{"id":"/library/exclusions","page_id":"/library/exclusions","type":"page","content":"Exclusions","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Library"],"tags":[],"url":"/library/exclusions"},"762":{"id":"/library/exclusions-0","page_id":"/library/exclusions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/library/exclusions","content":"Stop watchlisted titles from being requested, for one user or for everyone."},"763":{"id":"/library/exclusions-1","page_id":"/library/exclusions","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/library/exclusions#exclude-a-title","content":"Exclude a title"},"764":{"id":"/library/exclusions-2","page_id":"/library/exclusions","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/library/exclusions#exclusions-and-delete-sync","content":"Exclusions and delete sync"},"765":{"id":"/library/exclusions-3","page_id":"/library/exclusions","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/library/exclusions#maintainerr","content":"Maintainerr"},"766":{"id":"/library/exclusions-4","page_id":"/library/exclusions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/library/exclusions","content":"An exclusion stops Pulsarr requesting a title even though it's on someone's watchlist. The title stays on their watchlist in Plex. Manage exclusions under **Library** > **Exclusions**, which lists every title on any watchlist."},"767":{"id":"/library/exclusions-5","page_id":"/library/exclusions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/library/exclusions#exclude-a-title","content":"There are two kinds:"},"768":{"id":"/library/exclusions-6","page_id":"/library/exclusions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/library/exclusions#exclude-a-title","content":"**For one user.** Expand the title's row and select **Exclude** next to the user. **Remove** undoes it. This kind clears itself when the user removes the title from their watchlist, so adding it again later works normally."},"769":{"id":"/library/exclusions-7","page_id":"/library/exclusions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/library/exclusions#exclude-a-title","content":"**For everyone.** Select **Exclude for everyone** from the row's menu. It also blocks anyone who adds the title later, and it stays until you select **Remove global exclusion**."},"770":{"id":"/library/exclusions-8","page_id":"/library/exclusions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/library/exclusions#exclude-a-title","content":"To act on several titles, select their rows and use **Exclude** with **Their watchlisters** or **Everyone**, or **Remove** to clear every exclusion on them."},"771":{"id":"/library/exclusions-9","page_id":"/library/exclusions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/library/exclusions#exclude-a-title","content":"Use **Search titles** and the **User**, **Content type**, **Status** and **Exclusion** filters to find titles."},"772":{"id":"/library/exclusions-10","page_id":"/library/exclusions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/library/exclusions#exclusions-and-delete-sync","content":"Delete sync treats an excluded title as if nobody had it on their watchlist. That applies once every watchlister is excluded, or the title has an exclusion for everyone. Delete sync can then remove it, as long as its own settings and safety checks allow it. This is also how you stop a deleted title from being requested again while it's still on someone's watchlist."},"773":{"id":"/library/exclusions-11","page_id":"/library/exclusions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/library/exclusions#maintainerr","content":"Pulsarr can add exclusions for media that Maintainerr deletes, so stale watchlists don't request it again. It needs Maintainerr 3.23.0 or later, and Maintainerr must be able to reach Pulsarr."},"774":{"id":"/library/exclusions-12","page_id":"/library/exclusions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/library/exclusions#maintainerr","content":"In the **Maintainerr** section, turn on **Use Maintainerr**, enter the **Maintainerr URL** and save. Pulsarr then sets up a webhook named \"Pulsarr\" in Maintainerr and connects it to the rule groups whose collections delete media. Groups that only unmonitor aren't connected, because the webhook doesn't say which action ran. Pulsarr reconnects on its own every hour, and **Sync now** does it straight away."},"775":{"id":"/library/exclusions-13","page_id":"/library/exclusions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/library/exclusions#maintainerr","content":"**Exclude for** decides what Pulsarr adds when Maintainerr deletes a title:"},"776":{"id":"/library/exclusions-14","page_id":"/library/exclusions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/library/exclusions#maintainerr","content":"**Current watchlisters** adds one exclusion for each user who has it watchlisted. Someone who adds it later can request it again."},"777":{"id":"/library/exclusions-15","page_id":"/library/exclusions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/library/exclusions#maintainerr","content":"**Everyone** adds one exclusion that blocks it for all users."},"778":{"id":"/library/exclusions-16","page_id":"/library/exclusions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/library/exclusions#maintainerr","content":"Maintainerr only adds exclusions. Remove them on this page."},"779":{"id":"/library/exclusions-17","page_id":"/library/exclusions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/library/exclusions#maintainerr","content":"If you use Maintainerr this way, consider turning delete sync off and keeping your removal rules in Maintainerr, so only one tool removes content."},"780":{"id":"/library","page_id":"/library","type":"page","content":"Library","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Library"],"tags":[],"url":"/library"},"781":{"id":"/library-0","page_id":"/library","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/library","content":"Where requests go in Sonarr and Radarr, what's kept out, and what's removed."},"782":{"id":"/library-1","page_id":"/library","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/library","content":"These pages control what happens after a request leaves Pulsarr. They decide which instance gets it, which titles are never requested, and when content is removed."},"783":{"id":"/library-2","page_id":"/library","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/library","content":"<Card title=\"Sonarr and Radarr\" href=\"/library/sonarr-radarr\" description=\"Connect instances and set where content lands.\" />"},"784":{"id":"/library-3","page_id":"/library","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/library","content":"<Card title=\"Content router\" href=\"/library/content-router\" description=\"Send requests to different instances based on what they are and who asked.\" />"},"785":{"id":"/library-4","page_id":"/library","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/library","content":"<Card title=\"Exclusions\" href=\"/library/exclusions\" description=\"Stop watchlisted titles from being requested, including after Maintainerr deletes them.\" />"},"786":{"id":"/library-5","page_id":"/library","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/library","content":"<Card title=\"Delete sync\" href=\"/library/delete-sync\" description=\"Remove content from Sonarr and Radarr once nobody wants it.\" />"},"787":{"id":"/library-6","page_id":"/library","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/library","content":"<Card title=\"Session monitoring\" href=\"/library/session-monitoring\" description=\"Request the next season before people reach it, and grow rolling shows.\" />"},"788":{"id":"/library/session-monitoring","page_id":"/library/session-monitoring","type":"page","content":"Session monitoring","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Library"],"tags":[],"url":"/library/session-monitoring"},"789":{"id":"/library/session-monitoring-0","page_id":"/library/session-monitoring","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/library/session-monitoring","content":"Request the next season before people reach it, and grow rolling shows as they're watched."},"790":{"id":"/library/session-monitoring-1","page_id":"/library/session-monitoring","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/library/session-monitoring#monitoring","content":"Monitoring"},"791":{"id":"/library/session-monitoring-2","page_id":"/library/session-monitoring","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/library/session-monitoring#rolling-shows","content":"Rolling shows"},"792":{"id":"/library/session-monitoring-3","page_id":"/library/session-monitoring","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/library/session-monitoring#manage-enrollment","content":"Manage enrollment"},"793":{"id":"/library/session-monitoring-4","page_id":"/library/session-monitoring","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/library/session-monitoring#resets-and-cleanup","content":"Resets and cleanup"},"794":{"id":"/library/session-monitoring-5","page_id":"/library/session-monitoring","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/library/session-monitoring","content":"Session monitoring reads what's playing on Plex. When someone nears the end of a season, Pulsarr asks Sonarr for the next one. It also grows rolling shows as people watch them. Set it up under **Library** > **Session monitoring**."},"795":{"id":"/library/session-monitoring-6","page_id":"/library/session-monitoring","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/library/session-monitoring#monitoring","content":"Turn on **Session monitoring**, then set:"},"796":{"id":"/library/session-monitoring-7","page_id":"/library/session-monitoring","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/library/session-monitoring#monitoring","content":"**Remaining episodes threshold**. Pulsarr requests the next season when this many episodes of the current one are left."},"797":{"id":"/library/session-monitoring-8","page_id":"/library/session-monitoring","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/library/session-monitoring#monitoring","content":"**Monitored users**. Leave it empty to monitor everyone."},"798":{"id":"/library/session-monitoring-9","page_id":"/library/session-monitoring","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/library/session-monitoring#monitoring","content":"**Polling interval**. Pulsarr normally gets playback from the live Plex connection, and only polls at this interval while that connection is down."},"799":{"id":"/library/session-monitoring-10","page_id":"/library/session-monitoring","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/library/session-monitoring#monitoring","content":"**Check now** reads what's playing on Plex straight away."},"800":{"id":"/library/session-monitoring-11","page_id":"/library/session-monitoring","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/library/session-monitoring#rolling-shows","content":"A rolling show starts small in Sonarr and grows as people watch it. Pick a rolling mode as the **Season monitoring** of a Sonarr instance or a Content router route, or enroll shows already in Sonarr with **Manage enrollment**."},"801":{"id":"/library/session-monitoring-12","page_id":"/library/session-monitoring","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/library/session-monitoring#rolling-shows","content":"**Pilot rolling** starts with the first episode. Watching it adds the rest of the season, and later seasons are added as viewers near the end of each one."},"802":{"id":"/library/session-monitoring-13","page_id":"/library/session-monitoring","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/library/session-monitoring#rolling-shows","content":"**First season rolling** starts with the whole first season, then adds later seasons the same way."},"803":{"id":"/library/session-monitoring-14","page_id":"/library/session-monitoring","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/library/session-monitoring#rolling-shows","content":"**All seasons pilot rolling** starts with the first episode of every season. Watching a season's first episode adds the rest of that season, in any order."},"804":{"id":"/library/session-monitoring-15","page_id":"/library/session-monitoring","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/library/session-monitoring#rolling-shows","content":"Shows only grow while session monitoring is on."},"805":{"id":"/library/session-monitoring-16","page_id":"/library/session-monitoring","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/library/session-monitoring#manage-enrollment","content":"**Manage enrollment** lists the shows Pulsarr sent to Sonarr. Select shows, pick a **Rolling mode** and apply it. Enrolled shows keep their progress unless you turn on **Start over from the beginning**, which unmonitors every episode and deletes the files beyond the mode's starting point."},"806":{"id":"/library/session-monitoring-17","page_id":"/library/session-monitoring","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/library/session-monitoring#manage-enrollment","content":"The **Rolling shows** table shows each show's mode, season, viewers and last activity. From a show you can:"},"807":{"id":"/library/session-monitoring-18","page_id":"/library/session-monitoring","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/library/session-monitoring#manage-enrollment","content":"**Reset** it to its mode's starting point. Episode files rolling added are deleted and viewing progress is cleared."},"808":{"id":"/library/session-monitoring-19","page_id":"/library/session-monitoring","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/library/session-monitoring#manage-enrollment","content":"**Stop rolling**. Pulsarr stops tracking the show and nothing is deleted. The episodes stay in Sonarr."},"809":{"id":"/library/session-monitoring-20","page_id":"/library/session-monitoring","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/library/session-monitoring#resets-and-cleanup","content":"These decide what happens to shows nobody is watching:"},"810":{"id":"/library/session-monitoring-21","page_id":"/library/session-monitoring","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/library/session-monitoring#resets-and-cleanup","content":"**Automatic reset** resets shows that nobody has watched for the **Inactivity period**. **Check every** sets how often Pulsarr looks for them."},"811":{"id":"/library/session-monitoring-22","page_id":"/library/session-monitoring","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/library/session-monitoring#resets-and-cleanup","content":"**Progressive cleanup** deletes earlier seasons once no viewer is still on them."},"812":{"id":"/library/session-monitoring-23","page_id":"/library/session-monitoring","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/library/session-monitoring#resets-and-cleanup","content":"When some shows are inactive, the **Rolling shows** card has a button that resets all of them at once, for example **Reset 3 inactive**."},"813":{"id":"/library/sonarr-radarr","page_id":"/library/sonarr-radarr","type":"page","content":"Sonarr and Radarr","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Library"],"tags":[],"url":"/library/sonarr-radarr"},"814":{"id":"/library/sonarr-radarr-0","page_id":"/library/sonarr-radarr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/library/sonarr-radarr","content":"Connect Sonarr and Radarr instances, set where content lands, and copy content between instances."},"815":{"id":"/library/sonarr-radarr-1","page_id":"/library/sonarr-radarr","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/library/sonarr-radarr#add-an-instance","content":"Add an instance"},"816":{"id":"/library/sonarr-radarr-2","page_id":"/library/sonarr-radarr","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/library/sonarr-radarr#where-content-lands","content":"Where content lands"},"817":{"id":"/library/sonarr-radarr-3","page_id":"/library/sonarr-radarr","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/library/sonarr-radarr#the-default-instance","content":"The default instance"},"818":{"id":"/library/sonarr-radarr-4","page_id":"/library/sonarr-radarr","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/library/sonarr-radarr#remove-an-instance","content":"Remove an instance"},"819":{"id":"/library/sonarr-radarr-5","page_id":"/library/sonarr-radarr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/library/sonarr-radarr","content":"Shows go to Sonarr and movies go to Radarr. Manage them under **Library** > **Sonarr** and **Library** > **Radarr**. Both pages work the same way, and the differences are noted below."},"820":{"id":"/library/sonarr-radarr-6","page_id":"/library/sonarr-radarr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/library/sonarr-radarr#add-an-instance","content":"Select **Add instance**, then fill in **Connection**:"},"821":{"id":"/library/sonarr-radarr-7","page_id":"/library/sonarr-radarr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/library/sonarr-radarr#add-an-instance","content":"**Name** is shown across Pulsarr, for example in the Content router."},"822":{"id":"/library/sonarr-radarr-8","page_id":"/library/sonarr-radarr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/library/sonarr-radarr#add-an-instance","content":"**URL** is the instance's address, including the port."},"823":{"id":"/library/sonarr-radarr-9","page_id":"/library/sonarr-radarr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/library/sonarr-radarr#add-an-instance","content":"**API key** is in Sonarr or Radarr under Settings > General."},"824":{"id":"/library/sonarr-radarr-10","page_id":"/library/sonarr-radarr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/library/sonarr-radarr#add-an-instance","content":"Select **Test connection**. Pulsarr needs a passing test before it can save, and the test also loads the quality profiles, root folders and tags for the next section."},"825":{"id":"/library/sonarr-radarr-11","page_id":"/library/sonarr-radarr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/library/sonarr-radarr#add-an-instance","content":"The test also checks that Sonarr or Radarr can reach Pulsarr, which it needs to report finished downloads. If it can't, select **Fix the address** and choose how your servers reach Pulsarr. You can also change that address in the **Webhooks** section of the page."},"826":{"id":"/library/sonarr-radarr-12","page_id":"/library/sonarr-radarr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/library/sonarr-radarr#where-content-lands","content":"These settings apply to everything Pulsarr sends to the instance, unless a Content router route overrides them."},"827":{"id":"/library/sonarr-radarr-13","page_id":"/library/sonarr-radarr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/library/sonarr-radarr#where-content-lands","content":"For both:"},"828":{"id":"/library/sonarr-radarr-14","page_id":"/library/sonarr-radarr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/library/sonarr-radarr#where-content-lands","content":"**Quality profile** and **Root folder**."},"829":{"id":"/library/sonarr-radarr-15","page_id":"/library/sonarr-radarr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/library/sonarr-radarr#where-content-lands","content":"**Search on add** searches as soon as an item is added."},"830":{"id":"/library/sonarr-radarr-16","page_id":"/library/sonarr-radarr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/library/sonarr-radarr#where-content-lands","content":"**Tags** are added to every item Pulsarr sends here."},"831":{"id":"/library/sonarr-radarr-17","page_id":"/library/sonarr-radarr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/library/sonarr-radarr#where-content-lands","content":"**Bypass ignored** adds content even when it's on the instance's import list exclusions."},"832":{"id":"/library/sonarr-radarr-18","page_id":"/library/sonarr-radarr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/library/sonarr-radarr#where-content-lands","content":"For Sonarr:"},"833":{"id":"/library/sonarr-radarr-19","page_id":"/library/sonarr-radarr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/library/sonarr-radarr#where-content-lands","content":"**Season monitoring** picks which episodes to monitor. The rolling options, **Pilot rolling**, **First season rolling** and **All seasons pilot rolling**, start small and monitor more as people watch. They only grow while session monitoring is on."},"834":{"id":"/library/sonarr-radarr-20","page_id":"/library/sonarr-radarr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/library/sonarr-radarr#where-content-lands","content":"**Series type** is **Standard**, **Anime** or **Daily**."},"835":{"id":"/library/sonarr-radarr-21","page_id":"/library/sonarr-radarr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/library/sonarr-radarr#where-content-lands","content":"**Monitor new items** decides whether seasons that air later are monitored."},"836":{"id":"/library/sonarr-radarr-22","page_id":"/library/sonarr-radarr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/library/sonarr-radarr#where-content-lands","content":"**Season folders** puts each season in its own folder."},"837":{"id":"/library/sonarr-radarr-23","page_id":"/library/sonarr-radarr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/library/sonarr-radarr#where-content-lands","content":"For Radarr:"},"838":{"id":"/library/sonarr-radarr-24","page_id":"/library/sonarr-radarr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/library/sonarr-radarr#where-content-lands","content":"**Minimum availability** is **Announced**, **In cinemas** or **Released**."},"839":{"id":"/library/sonarr-radarr-25","page_id":"/library/sonarr-radarr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/library/sonarr-radarr#where-content-lands","content":"**Monitor** is **Movie only**, **Movie and collection** or **None**."},"840":{"id":"/library/sonarr-radarr-26","page_id":"/library/sonarr-radarr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/library/sonarr-radarr#the-default-instance","content":"Content that no Content router route claims goes to the **Default instance**. There's one default per type, and the first instance you add is always the default."},"841":{"id":"/library/sonarr-radarr-27","page_id":"/library/sonarr-radarr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/library/sonarr-radarr#the-default-instance","content":"Only the default instance has these two settings:"},"842":{"id":"/library/sonarr-radarr-28","page_id":"/library/sonarr-radarr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/library/sonarr-radarr#the-default-instance","content":"**Synced instances** also receive everything that reaches the default, for example to keep a 4K copy. Each synced instance uses its own settings."},"843":{"id":"/library/sonarr-radarr-29","page_id":"/library/sonarr-radarr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/library/sonarr-radarr#the-default-instance","content":"**Skip content no route matches**, when on, skips content that no route claims instead of sending it to the default."},"844":{"id":"/library/sonarr-radarr-30","page_id":"/library/sonarr-radarr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/library/sonarr-radarr#the-default-instance","content":"When you add a synced instance, **Copy existing content** sends everything already on the default to it. New content syncs on its own."},"845":{"id":"/library/sonarr-radarr-31","page_id":"/library/sonarr-radarr","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/library/sonarr-radarr#remove-an-instance","content":"Removing an instance also deletes the Content router routes that send to it, its place in other instances' synced instances, and Pulsarr's record of which watchlist items are on it. The watchlist items themselves stay. For Sonarr, rolling monitored shows on the instance are removed too."},"846":{"id":"/notifications/apprise","page_id":"/notifications/apprise","type":"page","content":"Apprise","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Notifications"],"tags":[],"url":"/notifications/apprise"},"847":{"id":"/notifications/apprise-0","page_id":"/notifications/apprise","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/notifications/apprise","content":"Send notifications to Telegram, Slack, email and many other services through an Apprise server."},"848":{"id":"/notifications/apprise-1","page_id":"/notifications/apprise","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/notifications/apprise#run-apprise","content":"Run Apprise"},"849":{"id":"/notifications/apprise-2","page_id":"/notifications/apprise","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/notifications/apprise#system-notifications","content":"System notifications"},"850":{"id":"/notifications/apprise-3","page_id":"/notifications/apprise","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/notifications/apprise#users","content":"Users"},"851":{"id":"/notifications/apprise-4","page_id":"/notifications/apprise","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/notifications/apprise#email-addresses","content":"Email addresses"},"852":{"id":"/notifications/apprise-5","page_id":"/notifications/apprise","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/notifications/apprise#saved-apprise-configs","content":"Saved Apprise configs"},"853":{"id":"/notifications/apprise-6","page_id":"/notifications/apprise","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/notifications/apprise","content":"Apprise sends notifications to many services, such as Telegram, Slack and email. Each destination is an Apprise URL in that service's own format. Pulsarr sends each notification to your Apprise API server along with the URLs it should go to, and Apprise delivers it. Users can get their own notifications through it, and admins can get system notifications."},"854":{"id":"/notifications/apprise-7","page_id":"/notifications/apprise","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/notifications/apprise#run-apprise","content":"Run the Apprise API container in the same Compose file as Pulsarr, so Pulsarr can reach it by name:"},"855":{"id":"/notifications/apprise-8","page_id":"/notifications/apprise","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/notifications/apprise#run-apprise","content":"Then point Pulsarr at it in `.env` and restart Pulsarr:"},"856":{"id":"/notifications/apprise-9","page_id":"/notifications/apprise","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/notifications/apprise#run-apprise","content":"If Apprise runs somewhere else, use its full address instead, for example `http://192.168.1.100:8000`. Pulsarr reads `appriseUrl` only at startup. **Notifications** > **Apprise** shows the address in use and whether Pulsarr can reach it."},"857":{"id":"/notifications/apprise-10","page_id":"/notifications/apprise","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/notifications/apprise#system-notifications","content":"**Apprise URLs** under **System notifications** is where admin notifications go. Enter an Apprise URL, for example `tgram://bot_token/chat_id`, and select **Add URL** for each extra one. With an email sender set, a plain email address works too. The Apprise documentation lists the URL format for every service."},"858":{"id":"/notifications/apprise-11","page_id":"/notifications/apprise","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/notifications/apprise#system-notifications","content":"**Send test** next to a URL sends a test notification to it, and **Test saved URLs** tests the URLs already saved."},"859":{"id":"/notifications/apprise-12","page_id":"/notifications/apprise","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/notifications/apprise#users","content":"A user's own Apprise URL goes on their page under Plex users, or they can set it with `/notifications` in Discord."},"860":{"id":"/notifications/apprise-13","page_id":"/notifications/apprise","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/notifications/apprise#email-addresses","content":"**Email sender** takes a `mailtos://` URL for an account that can send mail, for example `mailtos://user:app_password@gmail.com`. With it set, any Apprise field in Pulsarr also accepts a plain email address, and Pulsarr sends to it through that account. Gmail needs an app password. The email sender doesn't work with saved Apprise configs."},"861":{"id":"/notifications/apprise-14","page_id":"/notifications/apprise","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/notifications/apprise#saved-apprise-configs","content":"Pulsarr uses Apprise's stateless notify endpoint, so every URL you enter in Pulsarr is sent along with each notification, and nothing has to be saved in Apprise."},"862":{"id":"/notifications/apprise-15","page_id":"/notifications/apprise","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/notifications/apprise#saved-apprise-configs","content":"If you already keep your services in a config saved in Apprise, you can point Pulsarr at it instead. Saved configs need Apprise's stateful mode, which `APPRISE_STATEFUL_MODE=simple` in the example above turns on. Enter `apprise://apprise:8000/<config-key>` wherever Pulsarr takes an Apprise URL, or `apprises://` when Apprise is behind HTTPS. Add `?tags=` to send to only part of the config."},"863":{"id":"/notifications/apprise-16","page_id":"/notifications/apprise","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/notifications/apprise#saved-apprise-configs","content":"Two things work differently with a saved config:"},"864":{"id":"/notifications/apprise-17","page_id":"/notifications/apprise","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/notifications/apprise#saved-apprise-configs","content":"The **Email sender** doesn't work with saved configs. Put the email service in the saved config itself."},"865":{"id":"/notifications/apprise-18","page_id":"/notifications/apprise","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/notifications/apprise#saved-apprise-configs","content":"Posters and other images only come through with Apprise API 1.5.0 or later."},"866":{"id":"/notifications/delivery","page_id":"/notifications/delivery","type":"page","content":"Delivery","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Notifications"],"tags":[],"url":"/notifications/delivery"},"867":{"id":"/notifications/delivery-0","page_id":"/notifications/delivery","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/notifications/delivery","content":"Group episodes into fewer notifications, and choose where admin and user notifications go."},"868":{"id":"/notifications/delivery-1","page_id":"/notifications/delivery","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/notifications/delivery#episode-grouping","content":"Episode grouping"},"869":{"id":"/notifications/delivery-2","page_id":"/notifications/delivery","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/notifications/delivery#admin-notifications","content":"Admin notifications"},"870":{"id":"/notifications/delivery-3","page_id":"/notifications/delivery","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/notifications/delivery#user-notifications","content":"User notifications"},"871":{"id":"/notifications/delivery-4","page_id":"/notifications/delivery","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/notifications/delivery","content":"These settings apply to every notification channel. Find them under **Notifications** > **Delivery**."},"872":{"id":"/notifications/delivery-5","page_id":"/notifications/delivery","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/notifications/delivery#episode-grouping","content":"When several episodes of a show arrive close together, Pulsarr sends one notification instead of one per episode."},"873":{"id":"/notifications/delivery-6","page_id":"/notifications/delivery","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/notifications/delivery#episode-grouping","content":"**Queue wait time** is how long Pulsarr waits to collect episodes before it sends."},"874":{"id":"/notifications/delivery-7","page_id":"/notifications/delivery","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/notifications/delivery#episode-grouping","content":"**New episode threshold** is how recently an episode must have aired to skip the wait and notify straight away. Older episodes, such as a back catalog being imported, are grouped."},"875":{"id":"/notifications/delivery-8","page_id":"/notifications/delivery","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/notifications/delivery#admin-notifications","content":"These pick where notices for admins go. The choices are **All channels**, **Apprise only**, **Discord webhook and direct messages**, **Discord direct messages only**, **Discord webhook only** and **None**."},"876":{"id":"/notifications/delivery-9","page_id":"/notifications/delivery","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/notifications/delivery#admin-notifications","content":"**Watchlist additions** tells you when a user adds something."},"877":{"id":"/notifications/delivery-10","page_id":"/notifications/delivery","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/notifications/delivery#admin-notifications","content":"**Update notifications** tells you when a new Pulsarr release comes out. Pulsarr never updates itself."},"878":{"id":"/notifications/delivery-11","page_id":"/notifications/delivery","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/notifications/delivery#admin-notifications","content":"Webhook delivery uses the Discord admin webhooks, direct messages need the Discord bot, and Apprise uses the Apprise system notifications."},"879":{"id":"/notifications/delivery-12","page_id":"/notifications/delivery","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/notifications/delivery#user-notifications","content":"**Availability notifications** decides whether users are told when something they asked for is ready. Each user still picks their own channels on their page under Plex users."},"880":{"id":"/notifications/discord","page_id":"/notifications/discord","type":"page","content":"Discord","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Notifications"],"tags":[],"url":"/notifications/discord"},"881":{"id":"/notifications/discord-0","page_id":"/notifications/discord","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/notifications/discord","content":"Post admin notifications to Discord channels, and message users through a bot."},"882":{"id":"/notifications/discord-1","page_id":"/notifications/discord","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/notifications/discord#admin-webhooks","content":"Admin webhooks"},"883":{"id":"/notifications/discord-2","page_id":"/notifications/discord","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/notifications/discord#discord-bot","content":"Discord bot"},"884":{"id":"/notifications/discord-3","page_id":"/notifications/discord","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/notifications/discord#create-the-bot","content":"Create the bot"},"885":{"id":"/notifications/discord-4","page_id":"/notifications/discord","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/notifications/discord#connect-it-to-pulsarr","content":"Connect it to Pulsarr"},"886":{"id":"/notifications/discord-5","page_id":"/notifications/discord","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/notifications/discord#link-users","content":"Link users"},"887":{"id":"/notifications/discord-6","page_id":"/notifications/discord","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/notifications/discord#approve-requests-from-discord","content":"Approve requests from Discord"},"888":{"id":"/notifications/discord-7","page_id":"/notifications/discord","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/notifications/discord","content":"Discord has two parts, set up under **Notifications** > **Discord**. Admin webhooks post Pulsarr's system notifications to channels. The Discord bot sends each user a direct message when something they asked for is ready, and lets them manage their own settings."},"889":{"id":"/notifications/discord-8","page_id":"/notifications/discord","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/notifications/discord#admin-webhooks","content":"In Discord, open the channel's settings, then **Integrations** > **Webhooks** > **New Webhook**, and copy its URL."},"890":{"id":"/notifications/discord-9","page_id":"/notifications/discord","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/notifications/discord#admin-webhooks","content":"Paste it into **Webhook URLs** in Pulsarr. To post to several channels, select **Add URL** and paste each one into its own field."},"891":{"id":"/notifications/discord-10","page_id":"/notifications/discord","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/notifications/discord#admin-webhooks","content":"**Send test** next to a URL posts a test message to that channel, and **Test saved URLs** tests the ones already saved."},"892":{"id":"/notifications/discord-11","page_id":"/notifications/discord","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/notifications/discord#create-the-bot","content":"In the Discord Developer Portal, create a new application. You can use the Pulsarr icon as its picture."},"893":{"id":"/notifications/discord-12","page_id":"/notifications/discord","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/notifications/discord#create-the-bot","content":"On the **Bot** page, turn on **Message Content Intent** and copy the bot token."},"894":{"id":"/notifications/discord-13","page_id":"/notifications/discord","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/notifications/discord#create-the-bot","content":"On **OAuth2** > **URL Generator**, select the `bot` and `applications.commands` scopes, and the **Send Messages**, **Embed Links** and **Use Slash Commands** permissions."},"895":{"id":"/notifications/discord-14","page_id":"/notifications/discord","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/notifications/discord#create-the-bot","content":"Open the generated URL and add the bot to your server."},"896":{"id":"/notifications/discord-15","page_id":"/notifications/discord","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/notifications/discord#connect-it-to-pulsarr","content":"Enter the **Bot token** and the **Client ID**, which is on the application's **General Information** page. Save, then select **Start bot**."},"897":{"id":"/notifications/discord-16","page_id":"/notifications/discord","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/notifications/discord#connect-it-to-pulsarr","content":"**Send a test direct message** messages one Discord user through the bot to check it works."},"898":{"id":"/notifications/discord-17","page_id":"/notifications/discord","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/notifications/discord#link-users","content":"Each user runs `/notifications` in your Discord server and enters their Plex username to link their account. After that, `/notifications` lets them change their own notification settings."},"899":{"id":"/notifications/discord-18","page_id":"/notifications/discord","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/notifications/discord#link-users","content":"You can also paste a user's Discord user ID on their page under Plex users. Users get direct messages only once a Discord ID is saved for them."},"900":{"id":"/notifications/discord-19","page_id":"/notifications/discord","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/notifications/discord#approve-requests-from-discord","content":"`/approvals` lets you browse, approve and deny pending requests from Discord. It only answers the Discord user saved on your own Plex user, the account that owns the server."},"901":{"id":"/notifications","page_id":"/notifications","type":"page","content":"Notifications","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Notifications"],"tags":[],"url":"/notifications"},"902":{"id":"/notifications-0","page_id":"/notifications","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/notifications","content":"Tell users when their requests are ready, and keep admins informed."},"903":{"id":"/notifications-1","page_id":"/notifications","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/notifications","content":"Pulsarr tells users when something they asked for is ready, and tells admins about requests, deletions and updates. Pick the channels that suit you."},"904":{"id":"/notifications-2","page_id":"/notifications","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/notifications","content":"<Card title=\"Discord\" href=\"/notifications/discord\" description=\"Admin webhooks, and a bot that messages users.\" />"},"905":{"id":"/notifications-3","page_id":"/notifications","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/notifications","content":"<Card title=\"Apprise\" href=\"/notifications/apprise\" description=\"Telegram, Slack, email and many other services.\" />"},"906":{"id":"/notifications-4","page_id":"/notifications","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/notifications","content":"<Card title=\"Webhooks\" href=\"/notifications/webhooks\" description=\"JSON payloads for Home Assistant, n8n or your own service.\" />"},"907":{"id":"/notifications-5","page_id":"/notifications","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/notifications","content":"<Card title=\"Plex mobile\" href=\"/notifications/plex-mobile\" description=\"Push notifications in the Plex app.\" />"},"908":{"id":"/notifications-6","page_id":"/notifications","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/notifications","content":"<Card title=\"Public content\" href=\"/notifications/public-content\" description=\"Announce every ready title in shared channels.\" />"},"909":{"id":"/notifications-7","page_id":"/notifications","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/notifications","content":"<Card title=\"Delivery\" href=\"/notifications/delivery\" description=\"Episode grouping, admin notices and user alerts.\" />"},"910":{"id":"/notifications/plex-mobile","page_id":"/notifications/plex-mobile","type":"page","content":"Plex mobile","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Notifications"],"tags":[],"url":"/notifications/plex-mobile"},"911":{"id":"/notifications/plex-mobile-0","page_id":"/notifications/plex-mobile","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/notifications/plex-mobile","content":"Push a notification to users' Plex app when something on their watchlist is ready."},"912":{"id":"/notifications/plex-mobile-1","page_id":"/notifications/plex-mobile","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/notifications/plex-mobile#turn-it-on","content":"Turn it on"},"913":{"id":"/notifications/plex-mobile-2","page_id":"/notifications/plex-mobile","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/notifications/plex-mobile#in-the-plex-app","content":"In the Plex app"},"914":{"id":"/notifications/plex-mobile-3","page_id":"/notifications/plex-mobile","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/notifications/plex-mobile","content":"Pulsarr can push a notification straight to a user's Plex app on iOS or Android when something on their watchlist becomes available. Tapping it opens the title in Plex. It needs Plex Pass on your server."},"915":{"id":"/notifications/plex-mobile-4","page_id":"/notifications/plex-mobile","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/notifications/plex-mobile#turn-it-on","content":"Under **Notifications** > **Plex mobile**, turn on **Send to Plex mobile apps**. Then turn on **Plex mobile** for each user on their page under Plex users, or for several at once with **Edit settings**."},"916":{"id":"/notifications/plex-mobile-5","page_id":"/notifications/plex-mobile","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/notifications/plex-mobile#turn-it-on","content":"**Send a test push** pushes to one user's Plex app to check it works."},"917":{"id":"/notifications/plex-mobile-6","page_id":"/notifications/plex-mobile","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/notifications/plex-mobile#turn-it-on","content":"If a title isn't in Plex yet when it's ready, Pulsarr keeps trying for up to 10 minutes."},"918":{"id":"/notifications/plex-mobile-7","page_id":"/notifications/plex-mobile","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/notifications/plex-mobile#in-the-plex-app","content":"Users need push notifications turned on in the Plex app, under **Settings** > **Notifications**."},"919":{"id":"/notifications/plex-mobile-8","page_id":"/notifications/plex-mobile","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/notifications/plex-mobile#in-the-plex-app","content":"Plex can also notify about every new item in a library, under **New Content Added to Library**. With that on, users get two notifications for the same title. Unchecking all libraries there leaves only Pulsarr's, which only cover what's on their watchlist."},"920":{"id":"/notifications/public-content","page_id":"/notifications/public-content","type":"page","content":"Public content","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Notifications"],"tags":[],"url":"/notifications/public-content"},"921":{"id":"/notifications/public-content-0","page_id":"/notifications/public-content","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/notifications/public-content","content":"Announce every title that becomes available in shared Discord channels and Apprise targets."},"922":{"id":"/notifications/public-content-1","page_id":"/notifications/public-content","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/notifications/public-content","content":"Public content announces every title that becomes available, whoever asked for it, in shared channels. It works alongside each user's own notifications. Set it up under **Notifications** > **Public content** and turn on **Broadcast to shared channels**."},"923":{"id":"/notifications/public-content-2","page_id":"/notifications/public-content","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/notifications/public-content","content":"Each tab, **All content**, **Movies** and **Shows**, has two lists:"},"924":{"id":"/notifications/public-content-3","page_id":"/notifications/public-content","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/notifications/public-content","content":"**Discord webhooks**, the webhook URLs of the channels to post in."},"925":{"id":"/notifications/public-content-4","page_id":"/notifications/public-content","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/notifications/public-content","content":"**Apprise**, Apprise URLs, or email addresses when an email sender is set. These need an Apprise server."},"926":{"id":"/notifications/public-content-5","page_id":"/notifications/public-content","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/notifications/public-content","content":"Movies and shows use their own tab's lists when they have any, and the **All content** lists otherwise. They never get both."},"927":{"id":"/notifications/public-content-6","page_id":"/notifications/public-content","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/notifications/public-content","content":"**Send test** next to a URL sends a test announcement to it, and **Test saved URLs** tests the URLs already saved."},"928":{"id":"/notifications/public-content-7","page_id":"/notifications/public-content","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/notifications/public-content","content":"On Discord, the announcement mentions the users who have the title on their watchlist, if they have **Discord mention** turned on and a Discord ID saved on their page under Plex users."},"929":{"id":"/notifications/webhooks","page_id":"/notifications/webhooks","type":"page","content":"Webhooks","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Notifications"],"tags":[],"url":"/notifications/webhooks"},"930":{"id":"/notifications/webhooks-0","page_id":"/notifications/webhooks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/notifications/webhooks","content":"Post a JSON payload to your own service, such as Home Assistant or n8n, when something happens in Pulsarr."},"931":{"id":"/notifications/webhooks-1","page_id":"/notifications/webhooks","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/notifications/webhooks#add-an-endpoint","content":"Add an endpoint"},"932":{"id":"/notifications/webhooks-2","page_id":"/notifications/webhooks","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/notifications/webhooks#events","content":"Events"},"933":{"id":"/notifications/webhooks-3","page_id":"/notifications/webhooks","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/notifications/webhooks#payloads","content":"Payloads"},"934":{"id":"/notifications/webhooks-4","page_id":"/notifications/webhooks","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/notifications/webhooks#delivery","content":"Delivery"},"935":{"id":"/notifications/webhooks-5","page_id":"/notifications/webhooks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/notifications/webhooks","content":"Webhooks post a JSON payload to a URL you choose when an event happens. Use them to connect Pulsarr to Home Assistant, n8n or your own scripts. Set them up under **Notifications** > **Webhooks**."},"936":{"id":"/notifications/webhooks-6","page_id":"/notifications/webhooks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/notifications/webhooks#add-an-endpoint","content":"Select **Add endpoint**, then fill in:"},"937":{"id":"/notifications/webhooks-7","page_id":"/notifications/webhooks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/notifications/webhooks#add-an-endpoint","content":"**Name**, for example \"Home Assistant\"."},"938":{"id":"/notifications/webhooks-8","page_id":"/notifications/webhooks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/notifications/webhooks#add-an-endpoint","content":"**URL**, where Pulsarr posts."},"939":{"id":"/notifications/webhooks-9","page_id":"/notifications/webhooks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/notifications/webhooks#add-an-endpoint","content":"**Auth header**, optional. Fill in both **Header name** and **Header value**, for example `Authorization` and `Bearer <token>`, and Pulsarr sends it with every request."},"940":{"id":"/notifications/webhooks-10","page_id":"/notifications/webhooks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/notifications/webhooks#add-an-endpoint","content":"The events to send. Pick at least one."},"941":{"id":"/notifications/webhooks-11","page_id":"/notifications/webhooks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/notifications/webhooks#add-an-endpoint","content":"**Send test** posts a test event, with `\"event\": \"test\"`, to the URL and header as typed. Save the endpoint when you're done."},"942":{"id":"/notifications/webhooks-12","page_id":"/notifications/webhooks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/notifications/webhooks#add-an-endpoint","content":"On each saved endpoint, **Enabled** pauses deliveries without deleting it."},"943":{"id":"/notifications/webhooks-13","page_id":"/notifications/webhooks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/notifications/webhooks#events","content":"| Event             | Label           | Sent when                                  |\n| ----------------- | --------------- | ------------------------------------------ |\n| `media.available` | Media available | A movie or show becomes available in Plex. |","table":"table-0"},"944":{"id":"/notifications/webhooks-14","page_id":"/notifications/webhooks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/notifications/webhooks#events","content":"| Event             | Label           | Sent when                                 |\n| ----------------- | --------------- | ----------------------------------------- |\n| `watchlist.added` | Watchlist added | A user adds something to their watchlist. |","table":"table-0"},"945":{"id":"/notifications/webhooks-15","page_id":"/notifications/webhooks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/notifications/webhooks#events","content":"| Event               | Label             | Sent when                                      |\n| ------------------- | ----------------- | ---------------------------------------------- |\n| `watchlist.removed` | Watchlist removed | A user removes something from their watchlist. |","table":"table-0"},"946":{"id":"/notifications/webhooks-16","page_id":"/notifications/webhooks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/notifications/webhooks#events","content":"| Event              | Label            | Sent when                       |\n| ------------------ | ---------------- | ------------------------------- |\n| `approval.created` | Approval created | A request is held for approval. |","table":"table-0"},"947":{"id":"/notifications/webhooks-17","page_id":"/notifications/webhooks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/notifications/webhooks#events","content":"| Event               | Label             | Sent when                             |\n| ------------------- | ----------------- | ------------------------------------- |\n| `approval.resolved` | Approval resolved | A held request is approved or denied. |","table":"table-0"},"948":{"id":"/notifications/webhooks-18","page_id":"/notifications/webhooks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/notifications/webhooks#events","content":"| Event           | Label         | Sent when                                        |\n| --------------- | ------------- | ------------------------------------------------ |\n| `approval.auto` | Auto approved | A request goes through without needing approval. |","table":"table-0"},"949":{"id":"/notifications/webhooks-19","page_id":"/notifications/webhooks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/notifications/webhooks#events","content":"| Event                   | Label                | Sent when                   |\n| ----------------------- | -------------------- | --------------------------- |\n| `delete_sync.completed` | Delete sync complete | A delete sync run finishes. |","table":"table-0"},"950":{"id":"/notifications/webhooks-20","page_id":"/notifications/webhooks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/notifications/webhooks#events","content":"| Event          | Label        | Sent when                |\n| -------------- | ------------ | ------------------------ |\n| `user.created` | User created | Pulsarr adds a new user. |","table":"table-0"},"951":{"id":"/notifications/webhooks-21","page_id":"/notifications/webhooks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/notifications/webhooks#events","content":"| Event               | Label                 | Sent when                           |\n| ------------------- | --------------------- | ----------------------------------- |\n| `quota.cap_reached` | Watchlist cap reached | A user reaches their watchlist cap. |","table":"table-0"},"952":{"id":"/notifications/webhooks-22","page_id":"/notifications/webhooks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/notifications/webhooks#payloads","content":"Every payload has the same envelope:"},"953":{"id":"/notifications/webhooks-23","page_id":"/notifications/webhooks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/notifications/webhooks#payloads","content":"`data` depends on the event. The webhook payloads in the API reference document each one, with examples."},"954":{"id":"/notifications/webhooks-24","page_id":"/notifications/webhooks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/notifications/webhooks#delivery","content":"Your endpoint must answer within 10 seconds. Pulsarr tries each delivery up to three times."},"955":{"id":"/requests/approval-queue","page_id":"/requests/approval-queue","type":"page","content":"Approval queue","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Requests"],"tags":[],"url":"/requests/approval-queue"},"956":{"id":"/requests/approval-queue-0","page_id":"/requests/approval-queue","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/requests/approval-queue","content":"Review the requests waiting for your decision, and look back at past ones."},"957":{"id":"/requests/approval-queue-1","page_id":"/requests/approval-queue","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/requests/approval-queue#why-a-request-waits","content":"Why a request waits"},"958":{"id":"/requests/approval-queue-2","page_id":"/requests/approval-queue","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/requests/approval-queue#review-a-request","content":"Review a request"},"959":{"id":"/requests/approval-queue-3","page_id":"/requests/approval-queue","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/requests/approval-queue#act-on-several-requests","content":"Act on several requests"},"960":{"id":"/requests/approval-queue-4","page_id":"/requests/approval-queue","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/requests/approval-queue","content":"The approval queue is under **Requests**. **Pending** lists requests waiting for a decision. **History** lists approved, denied and expired requests, and requests that never needed approval, marked **Auto approved**."},"961":{"id":"/requests/approval-queue-5","page_id":"/requests/approval-queue","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/requests/approval-queue#why-a-request-waits","content":"The **Trigger** column says why each request was held, for example \"Rule: Classics need approval\" or \"Monthly quota: 10 of 10 movies used\". There are three reasons:"},"962":{"id":"/requests/approval-queue-6","page_id":"/requests/approval-queue","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/requests/approval-queue#why-a-request-waits","content":"**Router rule**. A Content router route asked for approval."},"963":{"id":"/requests/approval-queue-7","page_id":"/requests/approval-queue","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/requests/approval-queue#why-a-request-waits","content":"**Manual flag**. The user has **Require approval** turned on."},"964":{"id":"/requests/approval-queue-8","page_id":"/requests/approval-queue","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/requests/approval-queue#why-a-request-waits","content":"**Quota exceeded**. The request put the user over their quota."},"965":{"id":"/requests/approval-queue-9","page_id":"/requests/approval-queue","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/requests/approval-queue#why-a-request-waits","content":"Use **Search titles** and the **Requested by**, **Content type** and **Trigger** filters to narrow the list. The **Trigger** filter has the three reasons above, plus **Content criteria** for the auto-approved requests in **History**."},"966":{"id":"/requests/approval-queue-10","page_id":"/requests/approval-queue","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/requests/approval-queue#review-a-request","content":"Select a request to open it. The review shows why it was held and where Pulsarr will send it."},"967":{"id":"/requests/approval-queue-11","page_id":"/requests/approval-queue","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/requests/approval-queue#review-a-request","content":"**Approve** sends it to the Sonarr or Radarr instance shown under **Where it will go**."},"968":{"id":"/requests/approval-queue-12","page_id":"/requests/approval-queue","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/requests/approval-queue#review-a-request","content":"**Deny** sends nothing and moves it to **History** as denied. You can add a reason for your records before you confirm."},"969":{"id":"/requests/approval-queue-13","page_id":"/requests/approval-queue","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/requests/approval-queue#review-a-request","content":"**Delete** removes the record without refusing anything. The title can come back as a new request, and anything already sent to Sonarr or Radarr stays there."},"970":{"id":"/requests/approval-queue-14","page_id":"/requests/approval-queue","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/requests/approval-queue#review-a-request","content":"To send it somewhere else, select **Edit routing**, make your changes and select **Save routing** before you approve. You can change the **Instance**, **Quality profile**, **Root folder**, **Tags** and **Search on add**, plus **Season monitoring** and **Series type** for a show, or **Minimum availability** and **Monitor** for a movie. Changes apply to this request only, and your instance defaults stay as they are. **Also send to** adds synced instances, which use their own defaults."},"971":{"id":"/requests/approval-queue-15","page_id":"/requests/approval-queue","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/requests/approval-queue#review-a-request","content":"Notes you add stay with the request and appear in webhook notifications. The requester never sees them."},"972":{"id":"/requests/approval-queue-16","page_id":"/requests/approval-queue","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/requests/approval-queue#act-on-several-requests","content":"Select requests with their checkboxes, then use **Approve**, **Deny** or **Delete** in the bar that appears."},"973":{"id":"/requests/approval-queue-17","page_id":"/requests/approval-queue","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/requests/approval-queue#act-on-several-requests","content":"You can also approve and deny requests from Discord with the bot's `/approvals` command."},"974":{"id":"/requests/approval-settings","page_id":"/requests/approval-settings","type":"page","content":"Approval settings","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Requests"],"tags":[],"url":"/requests/approval-settings"},"975":{"id":"/requests/approval-settings-0","page_id":"/requests/approval-settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/requests/approval-settings","content":"Decide what happens to requests nobody approves, where approval notifications go, and how long history is kept."},"976":{"id":"/requests/approval-settings-1","page_id":"/requests/approval-settings","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/requests/approval-settings#expiration","content":"Expiration"},"977":{"id":"/requests/approval-settings-2","page_id":"/requests/approval-settings","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/requests/approval-settings#notifications","content":"Notifications"},"978":{"id":"/requests/approval-settings-3","page_id":"/requests/approval-settings","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/requests/approval-settings#cleanup","content":"Cleanup"},"979":{"id":"/requests/approval-settings-4","page_id":"/requests/approval-settings","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/requests/approval-settings#approval-maintenance","content":"Approval maintenance"},"980":{"id":"/requests/approval-settings-5","page_id":"/requests/approval-settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/requests/approval-settings","content":"Find these under **Requests** > **Approval settings**."},"981":{"id":"/requests/approval-settings-6","page_id":"/requests/approval-settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/requests/approval-settings#expiration","content":"**Expire approval requests** closes pending requests that wait too long for a decision. **Expire after** sets how long a request can wait."},"982":{"id":"/requests/approval-settings-7","page_id":"/requests/approval-settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/requests/approval-settings#expiration","content":"**When a request expires** decides what happens next:"},"983":{"id":"/requests/approval-settings-8","page_id":"/requests/approval-settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/requests/approval-settings#expiration","content":"**Mark as expired** closes the request and sends nothing to Sonarr or Radarr."},"984":{"id":"/requests/approval-settings-9","page_id":"/requests/approval-settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/requests/approval-settings#expiration","content":"**Approve automatically** approves it and sends it where it was routed."},"985":{"id":"/requests/approval-settings-10","page_id":"/requests/approval-settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/requests/approval-settings#expiration","content":"**Approve automatically when a quota resets** approves requests held for quota, oldest first, once the user has room again. It works whether or not expiration is on."},"986":{"id":"/requests/approval-settings-11","page_id":"/requests/approval-settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/requests/approval-settings#notifications","content":"**Send approval notifications to** picks where admins hear about requests that need a decision. The choices are **All channels**, **Apprise only**, **Discord webhook and direct messages**, **Discord direct messages only**, **Discord webhook only** and **None**. Set up the channels themselves under **Notifications**."},"987":{"id":"/requests/approval-settings-12","page_id":"/requests/approval-settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/requests/approval-settings#cleanup","content":"**Delete expired records after** removes expired requests older than this from **History**. Cleanup only runs while **Expire approval requests** is on."},"988":{"id":"/requests/approval-settings-13","page_id":"/requests/approval-settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/requests/approval-settings#approval-maintenance","content":"Expiring requests, approving them when a quota resets, and cleaning up old records all happen in one maintenance job. **Run on a schedule** turns it on or off, and **Run every** sets how often it runs."},"989":{"id":"/requests","page_id":"/requests","type":"page","content":"Requests","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Requests"],"tags":[],"url":"/requests"},"990":{"id":"/requests-0","page_id":"/requests","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/requests","content":"Hold requests for your approval and limit how much each user can request."},"991":{"id":"/requests-1","page_id":"/requests","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/requests","content":"Pulsarr sends most watchlist items straight to Sonarr or Radarr. An item waits in the approval queue instead when the user requires approval, when it puts them over their quota, or when a Content router route asks for approval."},"992":{"id":"/requests-2","page_id":"/requests","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/requests","content":"<Card title=\"Approval queue\" href=\"/requests/approval-queue\" description=\"Approve, deny or reroute requests that are waiting.\" />"},"993":{"id":"/requests-3","page_id":"/requests","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/requests","content":"<Card title=\"Approval settings\" href=\"/requests/approval-settings\" description=\"Expiration, approval notifications and cleanup.\" />"},"994":{"id":"/requests-4","page_id":"/requests","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/requests","content":"<Card title=\"Quotas\" href=\"/requests/quotas\" description=\"Request limits and watchlist caps per user.\" />"},"995":{"id":"/requests/quotas","page_id":"/requests/quotas","type":"page","content":"Quotas","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Requests"],"tags":[],"url":"/requests/quotas"},"996":{"id":"/requests/quotas-0","page_id":"/requests/quotas","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/requests/quotas","content":"Limit how many movies and shows each user can request, and cap the size of their watchlist."},"997":{"id":"/requests/quotas-1","page_id":"/requests/quotas","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/requests/quotas#set-a-users-quota","content":"Set a user's quota"},"998":{"id":"/requests/quotas-2","page_id":"/requests/quotas","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/requests/quotas#how-periods-reset","content":"How periods reset"},"999":{"id":"/requests/quotas-3","page_id":"/requests/quotas","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/requests/quotas#usage-history","content":"Usage history"},"1000":{"id":"/requests/quotas-4","page_id":"/requests/quotas","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/requests/quotas#cap-notifications","content":"Cap notifications"},"1001":{"id":"/requests/quotas-5","page_id":"/requests/quotas","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/requests/quotas","content":"A quota limits how many requests a user can make in a period. Requests over the limit wait in the approval queue. A watchlist cap limits how many items a user can have at once. Items past the cap are skipped, not held for approval."},"1002":{"id":"/requests/quotas-6","page_id":"/requests/quotas","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/requests/quotas#set-a-users-quota","content":"Open a user from **Users** > **Plex users**. Movies and shows have separate quotas. To set quotas for several users at once, select them on **Plex users** and use **Edit quotas**. New users get the quotas set on New user defaults."},"1003":{"id":"/requests/quotas-7","page_id":"/requests/quotas","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/requests/quotas#set-a-users-quota","content":"**Limit requests** turns the quota on."},"1004":{"id":"/requests/quotas-8","page_id":"/requests/quotas","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/requests/quotas#set-a-users-quota","content":"**Quota period** is **Daily**, **Weekly rolling** or **Monthly**."},"1005":{"id":"/requests/quotas-9","page_id":"/requests/quotas","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/requests/quotas#set-a-users-quota","content":"**Requests per period** is the limit."},"1006":{"id":"/requests/quotas-10","page_id":"/requests/quotas","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/requests/quotas#set-a-users-quota","content":"**Bypass approval over the limit** sends requests over the limit straight through, and turns the cap off."},"1007":{"id":"/requests/quotas-11","page_id":"/requests/quotas","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/requests/quotas#set-a-users-quota","content":"**Cap the watchlist** and **Watchlist cap** set the most items the user can have on their watchlist."},"1008":{"id":"/requests/quotas-12","page_id":"/requests/quotas","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/requests/quotas#set-a-users-quota","content":"**Remove quotas** deletes the user's quotas and caps. It can also approve the requests their quota was holding."},"1009":{"id":"/requests/quotas-13","page_id":"/requests/quotas","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/requests/quotas#how-periods-reset","content":"**Daily** resets at midnight, server time."},"1010":{"id":"/requests/quotas-14","page_id":"/requests/quotas","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/requests/quotas#how-periods-reset","content":"**Weekly rolling** counts the requests from the last few days, today included. A request stops counting once it's older than the window."},"1011":{"id":"/requests/quotas-15","page_id":"/requests/quotas","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/requests/quotas#how-periods-reset","content":"**Monthly** resets at midnight, server time, on the day you choose."},"1012":{"id":"/requests/quotas-16","page_id":"/requests/quotas","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/requests/quotas#how-periods-reset","content":"Set the weekly window and the monthly reset day under **Requests** > **Quotas**:"},"1013":{"id":"/requests/quotas-17","page_id":"/requests/quotas","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/requests/quotas#how-periods-reset","content":"**Count requests from the last** is the weekly rolling window, in days."},"1014":{"id":"/requests/quotas-18","page_id":"/requests/quotas","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/requests/quotas#how-periods-reset","content":"**Reset on day** is the monthly reset day."},"1015":{"id":"/requests/quotas-19","page_id":"/requests/quotas","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/requests/quotas#how-periods-reset","content":"**When a month is too short** only matters for a reset day of the 29th or later. **Reset on the last day** resets on the month's last day, **Skip that month** waits for the next reset, and **Reset on the 1st** resets on the 1st of the following month."},"1016":{"id":"/requests/quotas-20","page_id":"/requests/quotas","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/requests/quotas#how-periods-reset","content":"To approve held requests automatically once a user's quota resets, turn on **Approve automatically when a quota resets** in Approval settings."},"1017":{"id":"/requests/quotas-21","page_id":"/requests/quotas","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/requests/quotas#usage-history","content":"Each request a quota counts is kept as a usage record. **Delete old usage history** removes records older than **Keep usage history for**. Keep them at least as long as your longest quota period, or requests that still count are deleted."},"1018":{"id":"/requests/quotas-22","page_id":"/requests/quotas","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/requests/quotas#usage-history","content":"**Quota maintenance** runs that cleanup. **Run on a schedule** turns it on or off, and **Run at** sets the time, in the server's time zone."},"1019":{"id":"/requests/quotas-23","page_id":"/requests/quotas","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/requests/quotas#cap-notifications","content":"**Send cap notifications to** picks where admins hear that a user reached their watchlist cap. **Notify the user** also tells the user, by Discord or Apprise if they use them."},"1020":{"id":"/system/account","page_id":"/system/account","type":"page","content":"Account","breadcrumbs":["Docs","System"],"tags":[],"url":"/system/account"},"1021":{"id":"/system/account-0","page_id":"/system/account","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/system/account","content":"Change the email, username and password of your Pulsarr admin account."},"1022":{"id":"/system/account-1","page_id":"/system/account","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/system/account","content":"Your admin account is the login for Pulsarr itself, separate from your Plex account. Open **Account settings** from the account menu at the bottom of the sidebar."},"1023":{"id":"/system/account-2","page_id":"/system/account","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/system/account","content":"**Profile** has the **Email** and **Username** you sign in with."},"1024":{"id":"/system/account-3","page_id":"/system/account","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/system/account","content":"**Password** takes a **New password** and **Confirm new password**. Leave both blank to keep your current one."},"1025":{"id":"/system/account-4","page_id":"/system/account","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/system/account","content":"Enter your **Current password** under **Confirm changes** to save any of them."},"1026":{"id":"/system/account-5","page_id":"/system/account","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/system/account","content":"To turn sign-in off, or skip it on your local network, set `authenticationMethod` in `.env`."},"1027":{"id":"/system/api-keys","page_id":"/system/api-keys","type":"page","content":"API keys","breadcrumbs":["Docs","System"],"tags":[],"url":"/system/api-keys"},"1028":{"id":"/system/api-keys-0","page_id":"/system/api-keys","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/system/api-keys","content":"Let other apps and scripts call the Pulsarr API."},"1029":{"id":"/system/api-keys-1","page_id":"/system/api-keys","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/system/api-keys","content":"An API key lets another app, such as Home Assistant or your own script, call the Pulsarr API. Manage keys under **System** > **API keys**."},"1030":{"id":"/system/api-keys-2","page_id":"/system/api-keys","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/system/api-keys","content":"Enter a **Name** that says what will use the key, then select **Create key**. **Copy key** copies it. Send it in the `X-API-Key` header with each request."},"1031":{"id":"/system/api-keys-3","page_id":"/system/api-keys","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/system/api-keys","content":"**Revoke** cuts off anything using a key straight away, and it can't be undone."},"1032":{"id":"/system","page_id":"/system","type":"page","content":"System","breadcrumbs":["Docs","System"],"tags":[],"url":"/system"},"1033":{"id":"/system-0","page_id":"/system","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/system","content":"The Plex connection, API keys, logs and your admin account."},"1034":{"id":"/system-1","page_id":"/system","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/system","content":"These pages cover Pulsarr's own connections and housekeeping."},"1035":{"id":"/system-2","page_id":"/system","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/system","content":"<Card title=\"Plex connection\" href=\"/system/plex-connection\" description=\"The Plex account and server, watchlist feeds and library refresh.\" />"},"1036":{"id":"/system-3","page_id":"/system","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/system","content":"<Card title=\"API keys\" href=\"/system/api-keys\" description=\"Let other apps and scripts call the Pulsarr API.\" />"},"1037":{"id":"/system-4","page_id":"/system","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/system","content":"<Card title=\"Logs\" href=\"/system/logs\" description=\"Read the log as it's written, and set how much it records.\" />"},"1038":{"id":"/system-5","page_id":"/system","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/system","content":"<Card title=\"Account\" href=\"/system/account\" description=\"Your admin email, username and password.\" />"},"1039":{"id":"/system/logs","page_id":"/system/logs","type":"page","content":"Logs","breadcrumbs":["Docs","System"],"tags":[],"url":"/system/logs"},"1040":{"id":"/system/logs-0","page_id":"/system/logs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/system/logs","content":"Read Pulsarr's log as it's written, and set how much it records."},"1041":{"id":"/system/logs-1","page_id":"/system/logs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/system/logs","content":"**System** > **Logs** shows Pulsarr's log as it's written. Use **Search lines** and the **Level** filter to find what you need."},"1042":{"id":"/system/logs-2","page_id":"/system/logs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/system/logs","content":"Under **Log settings**:"},"1043":{"id":"/system/logs-3","page_id":"/system/logs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/system/logs","content":"**Application log level** sets how much Pulsarr records, from `fatal` to `trace`. Raise it to `debug` when you're chasing a problem, and set it back afterwards. A `logLevel` set in `.env` replaces this every time Pulsarr starts."},"1044":{"id":"/system/logs-4","page_id":"/system/logs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/system/logs","content":"**Initial lines** is how many earlier lines load when you open the page."},"1045":{"id":"/system/logs-5","page_id":"/system/logs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/system/logs","content":"The log files themselves are in the `logs` folder of Pulsarr's data folder, for example `./data/logs` in Docker."},"1046":{"id":"/system/plex-connection","page_id":"/system/plex-connection","type":"page","content":"Plex connection","breadcrumbs":["Docs","System"],"tags":[],"url":"/system/plex-connection"},"1047":{"id":"/system/plex-connection-0","page_id":"/system/plex-connection","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/system/plex-connection","content":"Link the Plex account and server Pulsarr reads watchlists through, and set up library refresh."},"1048":{"id":"/system/plex-connection-1","page_id":"/system/plex-connection","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/system/plex-connection#plex-account","content":"Plex account"},"1049":{"id":"/system/plex-connection-2","page_id":"/system/plex-connection","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/system/plex-connection#plex-server","content":"Plex server"},"1050":{"id":"/system/plex-connection-3","page_id":"/system/plex-connection","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/system/plex-connection#watchlist-feeds","content":"Watchlist feeds"},"1051":{"id":"/system/plex-connection-4","page_id":"/system/plex-connection","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/system/plex-connection#plex-library-refresh","content":"Plex library refresh"},"1052":{"id":"/system/plex-connection-5","page_id":"/system/plex-connection","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/system/plex-connection","content":"**System** > **Plex connection** holds what you set up in the first two steps of setup, plus a few things you only need later."},"1053":{"id":"/system/plex-connection-6","page_id":"/system/plex-connection","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/system/plex-connection#plex-account","content":"Pulsarr reads watchlists through the Plex account that owns your server. To link a different account, select **Relink with Plex** and approve Pulsarr on plex.tv, or **Paste a token** if you already have one."},"1054":{"id":"/system/plex-connection-7","page_id":"/system/plex-connection","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/system/plex-connection#plex-account","content":"**Unlink** removes the account. Watchlist syncing stops until you link again, and your requests and settings stay."},"1055":{"id":"/system/plex-connection-8","page_id":"/system/plex-connection","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/system/plex-connection#plex-server","content":"**Connection** starts on **Automatic**, which lets Pulsarr pick the best connection to your server. Choose **Address** to enter it yourself. **Test connection** checks it."},"1056":{"id":"/system/plex-connection-9","page_id":"/system/plex-connection","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/system/plex-connection#plex-server","content":"**Skip content already on Plex** skips requests for titles your server or a shared server already has."},"1057":{"id":"/system/plex-connection-10","page_id":"/system/plex-connection","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/system/plex-connection#plex-server","content":"**Plex live connection** shows whether Pulsarr is getting live updates from your server. While it's down, Pulsarr polls Plex instead."},"1058":{"id":"/system/plex-connection-11","page_id":"/system/plex-connection","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/system/plex-connection#watchlist-feeds","content":"With Plex Pass, Pulsarr watches two RSS feeds, **Your watchlist feed** and **Friends' watchlist feed**, so new watchlist items arrive within seconds. Without Plex Pass, Pulsarr checks each watchlist on a schedule. **Generate feeds again** asks Plex for new feed URLs and replaces the old ones."},"1059":{"id":"/system/plex-connection-12","page_id":"/system/plex-connection","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/system/plex-connection#watchlist-feeds","content":"**Sync watchlists** reads your and your friends' watchlists from Plex again."},"1060":{"id":"/system/plex-connection-13","page_id":"/system/plex-connection","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/system/plex-connection#plex-library-refresh","content":"Sonarr and Radarr can tell Plex to refresh its library after they import something. **Set up** adds that Plex Media Server connection to every Sonarr and Radarr instance, and **Remove** takes it off all of them, including ones added by hand."},"1061":{"id":"/users","page_id":"/users","type":"page","content":"Users","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Users"],"tags":[],"url":"/users"},"1062":{"id":"/users-0","page_id":"/users","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/users","content":"Your Plex friends, what each one can request, and how their requests are tagged and labeled."},"1063":{"id":"/users-1","page_id":"/users","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/users","content":"Pulsarr adds your Plex friends as users on its own. These pages set what each user can do and mark their requests in Sonarr, Radarr and Plex."},"1064":{"id":"/users-2","page_id":"/users","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/users","content":"<Card title=\"Plex users\" href=\"/users/plex-users\" description=\"Sync, approval, notifications and quotas for each person.\" />"},"1065":{"id":"/users-3","page_id":"/users","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/users","content":"<Card title=\"New user defaults\" href=\"/users/new-user-defaults\" description=\"What users start with when Pulsarr first sees them.\" />"},"1066":{"id":"/users-4","page_id":"/users","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/users","content":"<Card title=\"User tags\" href=\"/users/user-tags\" description=\"Tag content in Sonarr and Radarr by who requested it.\" />"},"1067":{"id":"/users-5","page_id":"/users","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/users","content":"<Card title=\"Plex labels\" href=\"/users/plex-labels\" description=\"Label movies and shows in Plex by who has them on their watchlist.\" />"},"1068":{"id":"/users/new-user-defaults","page_id":"/users/new-user-defaults","type":"page","content":"New user defaults","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Users"],"tags":[],"url":"/users/new-user-defaults"},"1069":{"id":"/users/new-user-defaults-0","page_id":"/users/new-user-defaults","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/users/new-user-defaults","content":"Set what users start with when Pulsarr first sees them."},"1070":{"id":"/users/new-user-defaults-1","page_id":"/users/new-user-defaults","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/users/new-user-defaults","content":"Each time Pulsarr syncs, any Plex friend it hasn't seen before becomes a user with these settings. Changing them doesn't affect existing users. Edit those on Plex users. Find these under **Users** > **New user defaults**. You also set them during first-run setup."},"1071":{"id":"/users/new-user-defaults-2","page_id":"/users/new-user-defaults","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/users/new-user-defaults","content":"Under **Access**:"},"1072":{"id":"/users/new-user-defaults-3","page_id":"/users/new-user-defaults","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/users/new-user-defaults","content":"**Sync watchlist** is on by default. Turn it off to add new users without requesting what they watchlist."},"1073":{"id":"/users/new-user-defaults-4","page_id":"/users/new-user-defaults","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/users/new-user-defaults","content":"**Require approval** holds every request from new users in the approval queue."},"1074":{"id":"/users/new-user-defaults-5","page_id":"/users/new-user-defaults","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/users/new-user-defaults","content":"Under **Movies** and **Shows**, **Limit requests** gives new users a quota with a **Quota period** and **Requests per period**. **Bypass approval over the limit** sends their requests over the limit straight through. **Cap the watchlist** and **Watchlist cap** set the most items new users can have on their watchlist."},"1075":{"id":"/users/plex-labels","page_id":"/users/plex-labels","type":"page","content":"Plex labels","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Users"],"tags":[],"url":"/users/plex-labels"},"1076":{"id":"/users/plex-labels-0","page_id":"/users/plex-labels","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/users/plex-labels","content":"Label movies and shows in Plex by who has them on their watchlist."},"1077":{"id":"/users/plex-labels-1","page_id":"/users/plex-labels","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/users/plex-labels#labeling","content":"Labeling"},"1078":{"id":"/users/plex-labels-2","page_id":"/users/plex-labels","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/users/plex-labels#when-something-leaves-a-watchlist","content":"When something leaves a watchlist"},"1079":{"id":"/users/plex-labels-3","page_id":"/users/plex-labels","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/users/plex-labels#tag-sync","content":"Tag sync"},"1080":{"id":"/users/plex-labels-4","page_id":"/users/plex-labels","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/users/plex-labels#full-sync","content":"Full sync"},"1081":{"id":"/users/plex-labels-5","page_id":"/users/plex-labels","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/users/plex-labels#remove-labels","content":"Remove labels"},"1082":{"id":"/users/plex-labels-6","page_id":"/users/plex-labels","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/users/plex-labels","content":"Plex labels mark each movie and show in Plex with the users who have it on their watchlist. Set them up under **Users** > **Plex labels**."},"1083":{"id":"/users/plex-labels-7","page_id":"/users/plex-labels","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/users/plex-labels#labeling","content":"**Label content in Plex** labels each item with who watchlists it, once the item is in Plex. A label is the **Prefix** and the user's name, for example `pulsarr:jamie`. **Name from** picks **Username** or **Alias**."},"1084":{"id":"/users/plex-labels-8","page_id":"/users/plex-labels","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/users/plex-labels#labeling","content":"The format can't change while Pulsarr's labels exist. Remove them first with **Remove all Pulsarr labels**."},"1085":{"id":"/users/plex-labels-9","page_id":"/users/plex-labels","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/users/plex-labels#when-something-leaves-a-watchlist","content":"**Label behavior** decides what happens to a user's label when they remove the item:"},"1086":{"id":"/users/plex-labels-10","page_id":"/users/plex-labels","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/users/plex-labels#when-something-leaves-a-watchlist","content":"**Remove the label** removes it."},"1087":{"id":"/users/plex-labels-11","page_id":"/users/plex-labels","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/users/plex-labels#when-something-leaves-a-watchlist","content":"**Keep the label** keeps it as a record of who asked."},"1088":{"id":"/users/plex-labels-12","page_id":"/users/plex-labels","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/users/plex-labels#when-something-leaves-a-watchlist","content":"**Swap for a removed label** replaces it with the **Removed label** once nobody wants the item, so you can find it."},"1089":{"id":"/users/plex-labels-13","page_id":"/users/plex-labels","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/users/plex-labels#when-something-leaves-a-watchlist","content":"**Clean up orphaned labels on sync** removes labels for users who were deleted, renamed or stopped syncing. **Reset labels before each sync** applies the rule above to leftover labels before each sync. Turn it on after you move away from **Keep the label**."},"1090":{"id":"/users/plex-labels-14","page_id":"/users/plex-labels","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/users/plex-labels#tag-sync","content":"**Sync tags as labels** copies Sonarr and Radarr tags to Plex as labels, except user tags. Each tag on an item becomes a label on it, with the same prefix. **Radarr tags on movies** and **Sonarr tags on shows** pick which ones."},"1091":{"id":"/users/plex-labels-15","page_id":"/users/plex-labels","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/users/plex-labels#full-sync","content":"**Full label sync** rechecks every watchlisted item and fixes its labels. It needs labeling on. **Run on a schedule** runs it at the time you set in **Run at**, in the server's time zone."},"1092":{"id":"/users/plex-labels-16","page_id":"/users/plex-labels","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/users/plex-labels#remove-labels","content":"**Clean up orphaned labels** deletes labels of removed, renamed or non-syncing users. **Remove all Pulsarr labels** strips every label Pulsarr added, user and tag labels alike. Other labels and your content aren't touched."},"1093":{"id":"/users/plex-users","page_id":"/users/plex-users","type":"page","content":"Plex users","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Users"],"tags":[],"url":"/users/plex-users"},"1094":{"id":"/users/plex-users-0","page_id":"/users/plex-users","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/users/plex-users","content":"Set sync, approval, notifications and quotas for each person."},"1095":{"id":"/users/plex-users-1","page_id":"/users/plex-users","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/users/plex-users#not-yet-friends","content":"Not yet friends"},"1096":{"id":"/users/plex-users-2","page_id":"/users/plex-users","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/users/plex-users#change-one-user","content":"Change one user"},"1097":{"id":"/users/plex-users-3","page_id":"/users/plex-users","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/users/plex-users#change-several-users","content":"Change several users"},"1098":{"id":"/users/plex-users-4","page_id":"/users/plex-users","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/users/plex-users","content":"**Users** > **Plex users** lists you, your Plex friends, and anyone with access to your Plex server. Pulsarr adds friends on its own, with your new user defaults."},"1099":{"id":"/users/plex-users-5","page_id":"/users/plex-users","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/users/plex-users","content":"The table shows each user's **Relationship**, **Watchlist** size, whether they **Sync**, whether they need **Approval**, their **Notifications** and their **Quotas**. Use **Search users** and the filters to narrow it."},"1100":{"id":"/users/plex-users-6","page_id":"/users/plex-users","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/users/plex-users#not-yet-friends","content":"Pulsarr can only read the watchlists of your Plex friends. People with access to your server who aren't friends, and pending friend requests, show under **Not yet friends**."},"1101":{"id":"/users/plex-users-7","page_id":"/users/plex-users","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/users/plex-users#not-yet-friends","content":"**No friend** has access to your server but isn't a Plex friend. Select **Send friend request**."},"1102":{"id":"/users/plex-users-8","page_id":"/users/plex-users","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/users/plex-users#not-yet-friends","content":"**Pending** is a request you sent that they haven't accepted. You can **Cancel request** or **Resend request**."},"1103":{"id":"/users/plex-users-9","page_id":"/users/plex-users","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/users/plex-users#not-yet-friends","content":"**Incoming** is a request they sent you. Accept it in Plex."},"1104":{"id":"/users/plex-users-10","page_id":"/users/plex-users","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/users/plex-users#not-yet-friends","content":"A friend whose **Watchlist** shows 0 may have an empty watchlist or a private one. Pulsarr can't tell which. See the quick start for the Plex privacy setting."},"1105":{"id":"/users/plex-users-11","page_id":"/users/plex-users","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/users/plex-users#change-one-user","content":"Select a user to open their page."},"1106":{"id":"/users/plex-users-12","page_id":"/users/plex-users","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/users/plex-users#change-one-user","content":"**Identity** shows their **Plex username**, which can't be changed here, and an **Alias** shown instead of it in Pulsarr and notifications."},"1107":{"id":"/users/plex-users-13","page_id":"/users/plex-users","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/users/plex-users#change-one-user","content":"**Access** has **Sync watchlist**, which requests what they add, and **Require approval**, which holds their requests in the approval queue."},"1108":{"id":"/users/plex-users-14","page_id":"/users/plex-users","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/users/plex-users#change-one-user","content":"**Notifications** has their **Discord user ID** and **Apprise URL**, and switches for **Discord**, **Discord mention**, **Apprise** and **Plex mobile**. **Send a test** sends through the channels saved for them."},"1109":{"id":"/users/plex-users-15","page_id":"/users/plex-users","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/users/plex-users#change-one-user","content":"**Movies** and **Shows** set their quota and watchlist cap."},"1110":{"id":"/users/plex-users-16","page_id":"/users/plex-users","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/users/plex-users#change-one-user","content":"The page also shows what's on their watchlist, their requests by status and their quota usage."},"1111":{"id":"/users/plex-users-17","page_id":"/users/plex-users","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/users/plex-users#change-one-user","content":"**Remove friend** ends the Plex friendship. Their Pulsarr record, watchlist and quotas are deleted at the next sync."},"1112":{"id":"/users/plex-users-18","page_id":"/users/plex-users","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/users/plex-users#change-several-users","content":"Select users in the table, then:"},"1113":{"id":"/users/plex-users-19","page_id":"/users/plex-users","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/users/plex-users#change-several-users","content":"**Edit settings** changes access and notifications for all of them. Fields left as is keep each user's current value."},"1114":{"id":"/users/plex-users-20","page_id":"/users/plex-users","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/users/plex-users#change-several-users","content":"**Edit quotas** sets or removes their quotas."},"1115":{"id":"/users/user-tags","page_id":"/users/user-tags","type":"page","content":"User tags","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Users"],"tags":[],"url":"/users/user-tags"},"1116":{"id":"/users/user-tags-0","page_id":"/users/user-tags","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/users/user-tags","content":"Tag content in Sonarr and Radarr by who requested it."},"1117":{"id":"/users/user-tags-1","page_id":"/users/user-tags","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/users/user-tags#where-to-tag","content":"Where to tag"},"1118":{"id":"/users/user-tags-2","page_id":"/users/user-tags","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/users/user-tags#tag-format","content":"Tag format"},"1119":{"id":"/users/user-tags-3","page_id":"/users/user-tags","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/users/user-tags#when-something-leaves-a-watchlist","content":"When something leaves a watchlist"},"1120":{"id":"/users/user-tags-4","page_id":"/users/user-tags","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/users/user-tags#actions","content":"Actions"},"1121":{"id":"/users/user-tags-5","page_id":"/users/user-tags","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/users/user-tags","content":"User tags mark each movie and show in Sonarr and Radarr with the users who have it on their watchlist. Set them up under **Users** > **User tags**."},"1122":{"id":"/users/user-tags-6","page_id":"/users/user-tags","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/users/user-tags#where-to-tag","content":"**Tag movies in Radarr** and **Tag shows in Sonarr** add a tag for each user who has the item on their watchlist."},"1123":{"id":"/users/user-tags-7","page_id":"/users/user-tags","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/users/user-tags#tag-format","content":"A tag is the **Prefix** and the user's name, for example `pulsarr-user-jamie`. **Name from** picks **Username** or **Alias**. Users without an alias fall back to their Plex username."},"1124":{"id":"/users/user-tags-8","page_id":"/users/user-tags","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/users/user-tags#tag-format","content":"The format can't change while the tags exist in Sonarr or Radarr. Remove them first with **Remove all user tags** and **Also delete the tag definitions**."},"1125":{"id":"/users/user-tags-9","page_id":"/users/user-tags","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/users/user-tags#when-something-leaves-a-watchlist","content":"**Tag behavior** decides what happens to a user's tag when they remove the item:"},"1126":{"id":"/users/user-tags-10","page_id":"/users/user-tags","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/users/user-tags#when-something-leaves-a-watchlist","content":"**Remove the tag** removes it."},"1127":{"id":"/users/user-tags-11","page_id":"/users/user-tags","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/users/user-tags#when-something-leaves-a-watchlist","content":"**Keep the tag** keeps it as a record of who asked."},"1128":{"id":"/users/user-tags-12","page_id":"/users/user-tags","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/users/user-tags#when-something-leaves-a-watchlist","content":"**Swap for a removed tag** replaces it with the **Removed tag**. Delete sync in tag based mode deletes content with that tag."},"1129":{"id":"/users/user-tags-13","page_id":"/users/user-tags","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/users/user-tags#when-something-leaves-a-watchlist","content":"**Clean up orphaned tags on sync** removes the tags of users who were deleted or renamed in Plex."},"1130":{"id":"/users/user-tags-14","page_id":"/users/user-tags","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/users/user-tags#actions","content":"**Sync tags** tags everything currently on a watchlist and clears tags that no longer apply."},"1131":{"id":"/users/user-tags-15","page_id":"/users/user-tags","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/users/user-tags#actions","content":"**Create missing tags** adds a tag in each instance for any user who doesn't have one yet."},"1132":{"id":"/users/user-tags-16","page_id":"/users/user-tags","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/users/user-tags#actions","content":"**Clean up orphaned tags** deletes tags left behind by users who were removed or renamed."},"1133":{"id":"/users/user-tags-17","page_id":"/users/user-tags","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/users/user-t