:117,"963":64,"964":99,"965":1078,"966":896,"967":9,"968":36,"969":35,"970":1031,"971":702,"972":898,"973":1127,"974":371,"975":461,"976":526,"977":707,"978":408,"979":368,"980":535,"981":43,"982":166,"983":65,"984":8,"985":7,"986":124,"987":32,"988":527,"989":815,"990":637,"991":775,"992":199,"993":200,"994":221,"995":786,"996":670,"997":914,"998":642,"999":1077,"1000":391,"1001":335,"1002":716,"1003":62,"1004":101,"1005":112,"1006":13,"1007":16,"1008":107,"1009":28,"1010":164,"1011":72,"1012":917,"1013":24,"1014":114,"1015":165,"1016":1028,"1017":499,"1018":100,"1019":125,"1020":343,"1021":398,"1022":1130,"1023":94,"1024":83,"1025":513,"1026":1037,"1027":363,"1028":667,"1029":359,"1030":511,"1031":116,"1032":964,"1033":1005,"1034":1019,"1035":213,"1036":197,"1037":210,"1038":196,"1039":681,"1040":787,"1041":148,"1042":1050,"1043":4,"1044":52,"1045":1002,"1046":733,"1047":672,"1048":731,"1049":738,"1050":1097,"1051":736,"1052":149,"1053":770,"1054":156,"1055":23,"1056":133,"1057":90,"1058":1123,"1059":146,"1060":924,"1061":1090,"1062":1132,"1063":758,"1064":216,"1065":212,"1066":224,"1067":214,"1068":700,"1069":918,"1070":502,"1071":1049,"1072":145,"1073":113,"1074":1051,"1075":734,"1076":665,"1077":666,"1078":1110,"1079":968,"1080":551,"1081":801,"1082":735,"1083":61,"1084":998,"1085":60,"1086":108,"1087":58,"1088":141,"1089":19,"1090":143,"1091":47,"1092":20,"1093":739,"1094":915,"1095":701,"1096":393,"1097":394,"1098":161,"1099":1010,"1100":762,"1101":80,"1102":84,"1103":51,"1104":334,"1105":897,"1106":49,"1107":0,"1108":82,"1109":74,"1110":1003,"1111":106,"1112":899,"1113":39,"1114":38,"1115":1085,"1116":966,"1117":1117,"1118":967,"1119":1111,"1120":345,"1121":1087,"1122":152,"1123":339,"1124":999,"1125":151,"1126":109,"1127":59,"1128":142,"1129":21,"1130":144,"1131":25,"1132":22,"1133":105},"orderedDocs":[[1107,"**Access** has **Sync watchlist**, which requests what they add, and **Require approval**, which holds their requests in the approval queue."],[803,"**All seasons pilot rolling** starts with the first episode of every season. Watching a season's first episode adds the rest of that season, in any order."],[730,"**Always require approval** holds matching requests in the approval queue, even from users who can request freely. **Approval reason** is shown to admins on the held request."],[823,"**API key** is in Sonarr or Radarr under Settings > General."],[1043,"**Application log level** sets how much Pulsarr records, from `fatal` to `trace`. Raise it to `debug` when you're chasing a problem, and set it back afterwards. A `logLevel` set in `.env` replaces this every time Pulsarr starts."],[857,"**Apprise URLs** under **System notifications** is where admin notifications go. Enter an Apprise URL, for example `tgram://bot_token/chat_id`, and select **Add URL** for each extra one. With an email sender set, a plain email address works too. The Apprise documentation lists the URL format for every service."],[925,"**Apprise**, Apprise URLs, or email addresses when an email sender is set. These need an Apprise server."],[985,"**Approve automatically when a quota resets** approves requests held for quota, oldest first, once the user has room again. It works whether or not expiration is on."],[984,"**Approve automatically** approves it and sends it where it was routed."],[967,"**Approve** sends it to the Sonarr or Radarr instance shown under **Where it will go**."],[939,"**Auth header**, optional. Fill in both **Header name** and **Header value**, for example `Authorization` and `Bearer <token>`, and Pulsarr sends it with every request."],[810,"**Automatic reset** resets shows that nobody has watched for the **Inactivity period**. **Check every** sets how often Pulsarr looks for them."],[879,"**Availability notifications** decides whether users are told when something they asked for is ready. Each user still picks their own channels on their page under Plex users."],[1006,"**Bypass approval over the limit** sends requests over the limit straight through, and turns the cap off."],[831,"**Bypass ignored** adds content even when it's on the instance's import list exclusions."],[731,"**Bypass user quotas** means matching requests don't count toward the requester's quota."],[1007,"**Cap the watchlist** and **Watchlist cap** set the most items the user can have on their watchlist."],[799,"**Check now** reads what's playing on Plex straight away."],[754,"**Clean up approval records** removes approval records for deleted content."],[1089,"**Clean up orphaned labels on sync** removes labels for users who were deleted, renamed or stopped syncing. **Reset labels before each sync** applies the rule above to leftover labels before each sync. Turn it on after you move away from **Keep the label**."],[1092,"**Clean up orphaned labels** deletes labels of removed, renamed or non-syncing users. **Remove all Pulsarr labels** strips every label Pulsarr added, user and tag labels alike. Other labels and your content aren't touched."],[1129,"**Clean up orphaned tags on sync** removes the tags of users who were deleted or renamed in Plex."],[1132,"**Clean up orphaned tags** deletes tags left behind by users who were removed or renamed."],[1055,"**Connection** starts on **Automatic**, which lets Pulsarr pick the best connection to your server. Choose **Address** to enter it yourself. **Test connection** checks it."],[1013,"**Count requests from the last** is the weekly rolling window, in days."],[1131,"**Create missing tags** adds a tag in each instance for any user who doesn't have one yet."],[776,"**Current watchlisters** adds one exclusion for each user who has it watchlisted. Someone who adds it later can request it again."],[413,"**Customize home** opens the cards as a board of rows. Drag a row by its handle to move it, or drag a card into another row. Full-width cards move with their row. **Hide** puts a card under **Hidden cards**, **Show** brings it back, and **Reset layout** restores the default. Changes apply as you make them. Select **Done** to close."],[1009,"**Daily** resets at midnight, server time."],[744,"**Decide by** sets what counts as no longer wanted:"],[751,"**Delete continuing shows** removes every other show."],[750,"**Delete ended shows** removes shows Sonarr marks as ended."],[987,"**Delete expired records after** removes expired requests older than this from **History**. Cleanup only runs while **Expire approval requests** is on."],[752,"**Delete files** also deletes the media files from disk."],[749,"**Delete movies** removes movies from Radarr."],[969,"**Delete** removes the record without refusing anything. The title can come back as a new request, and anything already sent to Sonarr or Radarr stays there."],[968,"**Deny** sends nothing and moves it to **History** as denied. You can add a reason for your records before you confirm."],[924,"**Discord webhooks**, the webhook URLs of the channels to post in."],[1114,"**Edit quotas** sets or removes their quotas."],[1113,"**Edit settings** changes access and notifications for all of them. Fields left as is keep each user's current value."],[860,"**Email sender** takes a `mailtos://` URL for an account that can send mail, for example `mailtos://user:app_password@gmail.com`. With it set, any Apprise field in Pulsarr also accepts a plain email address, and Pulsarr sends to it through that account. Gmail needs an app password. The email sender doesn't work with saved Apprise configs."],[777,"**Everyone** adds one exclusion that blocks it for all users."],[775,"**Exclude for** decides what Pulsarr adds when Maintainerr deletes a title:"],[981,"**Expire approval requests** closes pending requests that wait too long for a decision. **Expire after** sets how long a request can wait."],[802,"**First season rolling** starts with the whole first season, then adds later seasons the same way."],[769,"**For everyone.** Select **Exclude for everyone** from the row's menu. It also blocks anyone who adds the title later, and it stays until you select **Remove global exclusion**."],[768,"**For one user.** Expand the title's row and select **Exclude** next to the user. **Remove** undoes it. This kind clears itself when the user removes the title from their watchlist, so adding it again later works normally."],[1091,"**Full label sync** rechecks every watchlisted item and fixes its labels. It needs labeling on. **Run on a schedule** runs it at the time you set in **Run at**, in the server's time zone."],[722,"**Genres**. When a condition checks for anime, Pulsarr also looks the title up in the community anime list and adds an \"anime\" genre if it's there."],[1106,"**Identity** shows their **Plex username**, which can't be changed here, and an **Alias** shown instead of it in Pulsarr and notifications."],[727,"**IMDb rating**, with an optional **Minimum votes**, **RT critic score**, **RT audience score** and **TMDB rating**."],[1103,"**Incoming** is a request they sent you. Accept it in Plex."],[1044,"**Initial lines** is how many earlier lines load when you open the page."],[425,"**It checks limits.** A user past their watchlist cap is skipped. Some requests need your approval first, because of a route, the user's **Require approval** setting, or their quota. Those wait in the approval queue."],[423,"**It filters.** A title with an exclusion isn't requested. With **Skip content already on Plex** on, nor is anything your server already has."],[427,"**It notifies.** When Sonarr or Radarr finish importing, they tell Pulsarr through a webhook. Pulsarr then tells everyone who has the title on their watchlist, through their channels."],[424,"**It routes.** The Content router picks the Sonarr or Radarr instance, or several, and their settings. A Skip route stops the request here. With no matching route, the request goes to the default instance."],[426,"**It sends the request** to Sonarr or Radarr, which search and download as usual."],[1087,"**Keep the label** keeps it as a record of who asked."],[1127,"**Keep the tag** keeps it as a record of who asked."],[1085,"**Label behavior** decides what happens to a user's label when they remove the item:"],[1083,"**Label content in Plex** labels each item with who watchlists it, once the item is in Plex. A label is the **Prefix** and the user's name, for example `pulsarr:jamie`. **Name from** picks **Username** or **Alias**."],[1003,"**Limit requests** turns the quota on."],[805,"**Manage enrollment** lists the shows Pulsarr sent to Sonarr. Select shows, pick a **Rolling mode** and apply it. Enrolled shows keep their progress unless you turn on **Start over from the beginning**, which unmonitors every episode and deletes the files beyond the mode's starting point."],[963,"**Manual flag**. The user has **Require approval** turned on."],[983,"**Mark as expired** closes the request and sends nothing to Sonarr or Radarr."],[719,"**Match** decides whether a request must meet **All** of the conditions or **Any** of them. Each condition is a field, an operator and a value, for example **Year** **is above** 2000. **Add condition** adds another. **Add group** adds a nested set with its own **All** or **Any**. **Not** reverses a condition or a whole group."],[757,"**Max deletion** aborts a run that would delete more than this percentage of your library."],[838,"**Minimum availability** is **Announced**, **In cinemas** or **Released**."],[835,"**Monitor new items** decides whether seasons that air later are monitored."],[839,"**Monitor** is **Movie only**, **Movie and collection** or **None**."],[797,"**Monitored users**. Leave it empty to monitor everyone."],[1011,"**Monthly** resets at midnight, server time, on the day you choose."],[405,"**Most active** shows who requests the most."],[1109,"**Movies** and **Shows** set their quota and watchlist cap."],[821,"**Name** is shown across Pulsarr, for example in the Content router."],[937,"**Name**, for example \"Home Assistant\"."],[404,"**Needs your approval** lists requests waiting in the approval queue."],[874,"**New episode threshold** is how recently an episode must have aired to skip the wait and notify straight away. Older episodes, such as a back catalog being imported, are grouped."],[700,"**New user defaults.** Pulsarr adds users on its own. Each time it syncs, any Plex friend it hasn't seen before becomes a Pulsarr user with these settings. That includes everyone found by the first sync in the next step. **Sync watchlist** is on by default, so their watchlists are read. Turn on **Require approval** if you want to approve each request first, or **Limit requests** under **Movies** and **Shows** to give new users a quota."],[1101,"**No friend** has access to your server but isn't a Plex friend. Select **Send friend request**."],[412,"**Notifications** counts what was sent, and through which channels."],[1108,"**Notifications** has their **Discord user ID** and **Apprise URL**, and switches for **Discord**, **Discord mention**, **Apprise** and **Plex mobile**. **Send a test** sends through the channels saved for them."],[1024,"**Password** takes a **New password** and **Confirm new password**. Leave both blank to keep your current one."],[1102,"**Pending** is a request you sent that they haven't accepted. You can **Cancel request** or **Resend request**."],[801,"**Pilot rolling** starts with the first episode. Watching it adds the rest of the season, and later seasons are added as viewers near the end of each one."],[411,"**Placements by instance** shows where the router sent requests."],[756,"**Playlist protection** skips anything in a Plex playlist with the **Playlist name**, in any user's account. Each run creates the playlist for users who don't have it yet."],[695,"**Plex account.** Select **Sign in with Plex**, then **Open plex.tv/link** and approve the code. If you'd rather paste a Plex token, use **Paste a token**."],[724,"**Plex list**, a custom Plex list owned by the requester."],[1057,"**Plex live connection** shows whether Pulsarr is getting live updates from your server. While it's down, Pulsarr polls Plex instead."],[696,"**Plex server.** The connection starts on **Automatic**, which lets Pulsarr pick the best connection. Select **Test connection** to check it, then **Continue**. Choose **Address** only if you want to enter the server address yourself."],[798,"**Polling interval**. Pulsarr normally gets playback from the live Plex connection, and only polls at this interval while that connection is down."],[409,"**Popularity rankings** list the most watchlisted movies and shows. Select a title to see its details, where it streams, and its state in Pulsarr and in your instances."],[1023,"**Profile** has the **Email** and **Username** you sign in with."],[811,"**Progressive cleanup** deletes earlier seasons once no viewer is still on them."],[422,"**Pulsarr spots the change,** within seconds with Plex Pass, or within about 5 minutes without it. How changes are spotted explains how."],[828,"**Quality profile** and **Root folder**."],[873,"**Queue wait time** is how long Pulsarr waits to collect episodes before it sends."],[964,"**Quota exceeded**. The request put the user over their quota."],[1018,"**Quota maintenance** runs that cleanup. **Run on a schedule** turns it on or off, and **Run at** sets the time, in the server's time zone."],[1004,"**Quota period** is **Daily**, **Weekly rolling** or **Monthly**."],[699,"**Radarr.** The same as Sonarr."],[406,"**Recent requests** lists the latest requests with their status. You can filter by status and change the sort order."],[796,"**Remaining episodes threshold**. Pulsarr requests the next season when this many episodes of the current one are left."],[1133,"**Remove all user tags** strips every user tag from movies and shows. Your content isn't touched. **Also delete the tag definitions** removes the tags themselves from Sonarr and Radarr too."],[1111,"**Remove friend** ends the Plex friendship. Their Pulsarr record, watchlist and quotas are deleted at the next sync."],[1008,"**Remove quotas** deletes the user's quotas and caps. It can also approve the requests their quota was holding."],[1086,"**Remove the label** removes it."],[1126,"**Remove the tag** removes it."],[407,"**Request pipeline** counts requests at each stage. **Requested** means it's in Sonarr or Radarr with no file yet. **Grabbed** means it's downloaded but nobody has been told. **Notified** means it's ready and the user was told."],[408,"**Request to ready** shows how long movies and shows take to become available."],[1005,"**Requests per period** is the limit."],[1073,"**Require approval** holds every request from new users in the approval queue."],[1014,"**Reset on day** is the monthly reset day."],[807,"**Reset** it to its mode's starting point. Episode files rolling added are deleted and viewing progress is cleared."],[1031,"**Revoke** cuts off anything using a key straight away, and it can't be undone."],[962,"**Router rule**. A Content router route asked for approval."],[759,"**Run now** runs once with the saved settings. **Run on a schedule** runs it at the **Day and time** you choose. Deleting can't be undone, so do a dry run first."],[829,"**Search on add** searches as soon as an item is added."],[836,"**Season folders** puts each season in its own folder."],[833,"**Season monitoring** picks which episodes to monitor. The rolling options, **Pilot rolling**, **First season rolling** and **All seasons pilot rolling**, start small and monitor more as people watch. They only grow while session monitoring is on."],[897,"**Send a test direct message** messages one Discord user through the bot to check it works."],[916,"**Send a test push** pushes to one user's Plex app to check it works."],[986,"**Send approval notifications to** picks where admins hear about requests that need a decision. The choices are **All channels**, **Apprise only**, **Discord webhook and direct messages**, **Discord direct messages only**, **Discord webhook only** and **None**. Set up the channels themselves under **Notifications**."],[1019,"**Send cap notifications to** picks where admins hear that a user reached their watchlist cap. **Notify the user** also tells the user, by Discord or Apprise if they use them."],[891,"**Send test** next to a URL posts a test message to that channel, and **Test saved URLs** tests the ones already saved."],[927,"**Send test** next to a URL sends a test announcement to it, and **Test saved URLs** tests the URLs already saved."],[858,"**Send test** next to a URL sends a test notification to it, and **Test saved URLs** tests the URLs already saved."],[941,"**Send test** posts a test event, with `\"event\": \"test\"`, to the URL and header as typed. Save the endpoint when you're done."],[760,"**Send the run summary to** picks where each run's summary goes, dry runs included. **Only when something was deleted** skips the summary when a run deletes nothing."],[716,"**Send to Sonarr** or **Send to Radarr** sends it to the **Instance** you pick. The route has its own quality profile, root folder, tags and other settings. Leave any of them on **Use instance default** to keep the instance's setting. Tags you list replace the instance's tags."],[834,"**Series type** is **Standard**, **Anime** or **Daily**."],[1056,"**Skip content already on Plex** skips requests for titles your server or a shared server already has."],[843,"**Skip content no route matches**, when on, skips content that no route claims instead of sending it to the default."],[717,"**Skip** never sends it anywhere."],[733,"**Skip** routes always run first. A matching Skip route stops the request from going anywhere, whatever the other routes say."],[697,"**Sonarr.** Enter a **Name**, the **URL** and the **API key**, then select **Test connection**. Once it connects, pick a **Quality profile** and **Root folder** and select **Save and continue**."],[701,"**Start syncing.** Select **Sync watchlists** to read every watchlist once. When every row shows **Done**, select **Start workflow**. Leave **Start on launch** on so syncing starts again after a restart. The dialog closes and the sidebar shows **Sync running**."],[808,"**Stop rolling**. Pulsarr stops tracking the show and nothing is deleted. The episodes stay in Sonarr."],[726,"**Streaming services**, where the title streams in your TMDB region."],[1088,"**Swap for a removed label** replaces it with the **Removed label** once nobody wants the item, so you can find it."],[1128,"**Swap for a removed tag** replaces it with the **Removed tag**. Delete sync in tag based mode deletes content with that tag."],[1090,"**Sync tags as labels** copies Sonarr and Radarr tags to Plex as labels, except user tags. Each tag on an item becomes a label on it, with the same prefix. **Radarr tags on movies** and **Sonarr tags on shows** pick which ones."],[1130,"**Sync tags** tags everything currently on a watchlist and clears tags that no longer apply."],[1072,"**Sync watchlist** is on by default. Turn it off to add new users without requesting what they watchlist."],[1059,"**Sync watchlists** reads your and your friends' watchlists from Plex again."],[842,"**Synced instances** also receive everything that reaches the default, for example to keep a 4K copy. Each synced instance uses its own settings."],[1041,"**System** > **Logs** shows Pulsarr's log as it's written. Use **Search lines** and the **Level** filter to find what you need."],[1052,"**System** > **Plex connection** holds what you set up in the first two steps of setup, plus a few things you only need later."],[746,"**Tag based** deletes anything carrying the **Removal tag**, which comes from User tags. Matching ignores case. **Required tag pattern** is an optional regular expression, and when set, content also needs a tag that matches it."],[1125,"**Tag behavior** decides what happens to a user's tag when they remove the item:"],[1122,"**Tag movies in Radarr** and **Tag shows in Sonarr** add a tag for each user who has the item on their watchlist."],[830,"**Tags** are added to every item Pulsarr sends here."],[410,"**Top genres** and **Library mix** break down what gets requested."],[753,"**Tracked content only** limits deletion to content requested through Pulsarr."],[1054,"**Unlink** removes the account. Watchlist syncing stops until you link again, and your requests and settings stay."],[877,"**Update notifications** tells you when a new Pulsarr release comes out. Pulsarr never updates itself."],[822,"**URL** is the instance's address, including the port."],[938,"**URL**, where Pulsarr posts."],[723,"**User**, the person who requested it."],[1098,"**Users** > **Plex users** lists you, your Plex friends, and anyone with access to your Plex server. Pulsarr adds friends on its own, with your new user defaults."],[876,"**Watchlist additions** tells you when a user adds something."],[745,"**Watchlist based** deletes anything that isn't on any counted user's watchlist. With **Respect user sync settings** on, only the watchlists of users with sync on count."],[1010,"**Weekly rolling** counts the requests from the last few days, today included. A request stops counting once it's older than the window."],[1015,"**When a month is too short** only matters for a reset day of the 29th or later. **Reset on the last day** resets on the month's last day, **Skip that month** waits for the next reset, and **Reset on the 1st** resets on the 1st of the following month."],[982,"**When a request expires** decides what happens next:"],[725,"**Year**, **Language** and **Certification**."],[464,"`.env` holds your time zone and any other Pulsarr environment variables:"],[900,"`/approvals` lets you browse, approve and deny pending requests from Discord. It only answers the Discord user saved on your own Plex user, the account that owns the server."],[628,"`/opt/pulsarr/.env`"],[629,"`/opt/pulsarr/data/db/`"],[630,"`/opt/pulsarr/data/logs/`"],[83,"`/v1/progress` 