 Plex doesn't say so. It looks the same as an empty watchlist. They can change it from the privacy icon next to Watchlist on their Plex profile, or in the Plex web app under Settings > Account > Account Visibility & Activity Sharing."],[653,"Each platform also has a plain zip, such as `pulsarr-vX.Y.Z-linux-x64.zip`. Extract it anywhere and run `./start.sh`, or `start.bat` on Windows. On macOS, remove the quarantine flag first, as the zip's `README.txt` explains. To update, stop Pulsarr, then run `./update.sh` or `update.bat` with the path to the new zip. Each zip has a `README.txt` that covers running it as a service."],[621,"Each release includes builds for Linux, Windows and macOS with the runtime included, so there's nothing else to install. Download them from the latest release. After installing, open `http://<your-server>:3003`, or `http://localhost:3003` on the same machine, and continue with Create the admin account in the quick start."],[1017,"Each request a quota counts is kept as a usage record. **Delete old usage history** removes records older than **Keep usage history for**. Keep them at least as long as your longest quota period, or requests that still count are deleted."],[714,"Each route shows its conditions and where matching requests go. The switch on a route turns it on or off without deleting it."],[923,"Each tab, **All content**, **Movies** and **Shows**, has two lists:"],[1070,"Each time Pulsarr syncs, any Plex friend it hasn't seen before becomes a user with these settings. Changing them doesn't affect existing users. Edit those on Plex users. Find these under **Users** > **New user defaults**. You also set them during first-run setup."],[898,"Each user runs `/notifications` in your Discord server and enters their Plex username to link their account. After that, `/notifications` lets them change their own notification settings."],[747,"Either way, a title excluded for all its watchlisters, or for everyone, counts as unwanted. In tag based mode