ion and its requests card manage requests from Home Assistant."],[445,"The Content router decides which Sonarr or Radarr instance each title goes to, with which quality profile and root folder. Approvals and quotas let you control what gets added."],[398,"The dashboard you land on, with what needs your attention and how requests are flowing."],[817,"The default instance"],[940,"The events to send. Pick at least one."],[702,"The first Sonarr and the first Radarr you add become the default instances. Requests go to them until you add rules in the **Content router**."],[1084,"The format can't change while Pulsarr's labels exist. Remove them first with **Remove all Pulsarr labels**."],[1124,"The format can't change while the tags exist in Sonarr or Radarr. Remove them first with **Remove all user tags** and **Also delete the tag definitions**."],[622,"The install script needs `curl`, `unzip` and systemd, and supports x64 and arm64:"],[414,"The layout is saved in your browser, so each browser keeps its own."],[1045,"The log files themselves are in the `logs` folder of Pulsarr's data folder, for example `./data/logs` in Docker."],[1110,"The page also shows what's on their watchlist, their requests by status and their quota usage."],[684,"The Plex account that owns your Plex server."],[1033,"The Plex connection, API keys, logs and your admin account."],[462,"The Pulsarr image, `lakker/pulsarr`, is built for `linux/amd64` and `linux/arm64`. If this is your first install, the quick start walks through the same steps and then first-run setup."],[403,"The range menu, for example **Last 30 days** or **All time**, sets the period the activity cards cover."],[720,"The route above sends a movie to Radarr Kids when it's Animation or Family, or rated G or PG, and isn't Horror."],[468,"The same container without Compose, run from the folder with your `.env`:"],[1099,"The table shows each user's **Relationship**, **Watchlist** size, whether they **Sync**, whether they need **Approval*